WEBVTT

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.690
Let's Go!

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.130
Roll the royal!

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.490
Hurry up, get the lifeline

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.130
Draw the yard of the mizzen on the windward side

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.490
Sky was clear a moment ago

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.010
This is to be expected

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.210
The Grand Line is very temperamental

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.170
At this rate, our mast will break.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.010
I've already given the orders.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.490
Watch out for the cyclone.
It'll hit us before we even notice it.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.170
There are men on the lookout
on both ends of the ship.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.250
Where's the pirate ship we spotted
before the storm?

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.900
To the northwest.
11 o'clock.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.450
Distance 800.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.170
Did we get the mark on the flag?

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.450
Uh, yes...

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.410
What was it?
Hurry up and tell me.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.530
Yes, sir.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:13.370
A skull and crossbones
with a straw hat.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.450
What?!

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.130
They're the pirates we must capture

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:32.490
It's a small ship

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.410
But it is riding out the storm beautifully.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.810
She must have an excellent navigator.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.810
This is not the time to be impressed,
you idiot.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:42.250
Yes, sir!

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.130
<i>Everyone at the Navy Headquarter
is talking about this Straw Hat Pirates.</i>

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:55.210
<i>Monkey D. Luffy and his crew</i>

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:59.650
<i>In this bloody Golden Age of Pirates...</i>

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:02.890
<i>This is one obnoxious group of rascals</i>

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.730
Captain, you have a call
from headquarters.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:10.170
- At a time like this? Is it an emergency?
- Yes.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:12.890
They're on radio number 3.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:14.650
Are you serious?

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.730
Just as I just said.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.330
Pirates have gathered
in the seas right around you.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.690
For what?

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.170
I have no idea, but

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.720
It's probably for that
crazy bash again.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.490
That secret race?

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:30.650
Most likely

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:31.850
So that's why.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.690
We just spotted a pirate ship
a little while ago.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:35.770
Right.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.210
Keep watching the waters around you.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.090
A nasty name keeps coming up
in the stories we hear about this race.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.250
A nasty name?

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.690
Gusparday.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.500
That traitor?

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:47.010
That's right.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.050
The biggest disgrace to us Marines...

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.490
We can't let him run around loose anymore.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.810
In the name of absolute justice

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:09.690
The Adventure of Dead End

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.490
Wanna come with me?

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.210
<i>Hey...</i>

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.170
<i>...watch where you are going</i>

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.690
<i>Let's go for another drink</i>

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.080
<i>Let's drink until dawn</i>

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.970
Hey!
You think you can make fool out of me?

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:02.930
Boy, I'm full.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:04.610
You should be.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.090
If you eat that much

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.210
I can eat more

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.440
No, don't

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.970
The food was simple but good

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.370
Nami-san and Robin-chan,
do you want dessert?

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.780
No thanks.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:15.970
Coffee for me.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:17.530
Coming right up.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.330
- I want more.
- That's not fair!

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.530
You've had enough.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:22.450
- Ahhh!
- Don't "ah" me!

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.130
Somebody has to stop you,
or else you never will.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.890
- There you go.
- Thank you, Cook-san.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:31.410
Are we low on cash?

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.960
Well, we haven't seen
any booty lately.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.770
After we stock up on provisions,
we have no cash left.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.450
That's not good.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.680
How come?

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:42.290
Listen!
As your captain, let me say

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.490
you all are spending
way too much money!

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.890
It's mostly for your food!

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.610
But it's a serious problem.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.170
We need fast money.

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:56.330
Is there anything we can do here?

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.730
There's no casino on this island.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:03.690
We'll just have to hope
that we have better luck on next island.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.930
- What is it?
- Nothing.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.530
Give me some rum.

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:27.050
Thanks.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.040
Tell me something.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:32.770
This island is Hannabal,
isn't it?

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:33.850
Yeah...

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.130
Hm? What is it?

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:04.210
I don't know yet.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:07.770
The man who just came in.
He's probably a pirate.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.330
Something suspicious went on
between him and the shop owner.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:12.530
Right?

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.730
Zoro,
You were watching?

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.330
Not really.
Just caught a glimpse.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.050
- What do you think it is?
- What do you mean?

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:20.730
You know what I mean.
You smell something.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.770
Money that
you love so much.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.610
- Money?
- Hey!

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:27.450
You call me
a money monger?

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:28.570
And you're not?

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:29.880
Watch what you say to her.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.170
That I am!

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.640
I love money and mandarin oranges.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.250
Of course I saw what just went on.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:38.010
Luffy! Usopp!
Chopper!

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.370
I smell adventure.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.370
You guys can fight later.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.570
Excuse me.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:52.810
My friends and I could
always use a little more money.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:57.330
Do you know anything
we can do for big, fast bucks?

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:02.650
Oh, don't worry!
We have enough to pay for our bill here.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:04.130
It just seems...

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:06.860
there's something fun going on.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.010
You're still kids.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.010
But we're pirates.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.210
I thought you were.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:20.850
I've seen the “Wanted“ posters.

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.970
And I heard you guys talking about money.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:26.690
But you don't want to put
your lives at stake, do you?

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.530
No, we don't wanna do that.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:32.810
But we have so little money,
it's not even funny anymore.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.770
As the saying goes,
“nothing ventured, nothing gained.“

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:40.770
And we're outlaws anyway,
we don't have a legal source of income.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:42.730
And the treasure we're after is...

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.250
not easy to find.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:48.090
If we wanna make big money fast,

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:52.290
then of course we'll have to take some risks.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:55.730
We're used to breaking a few laws.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.770
We've been through so much.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:01.010
It's true we don't want to risk
our lives.

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:02.770
But the problem is

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.090
these guys are not the type of people

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:09.890
that back down
just 'cuz there's a little danger.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.370
Especially our captain.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:16.890
So please will you help us?

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.890
Tell us where we can find some money.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:24.890
There's no cure for fools and pirates...

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:26.770
-...You really want to rush to your death
- He's calling Zoro a Fool?

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:28.410
- Why me?
- Because, I'm the pirate.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.690
Follow me.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:32.450
All RIGHT!

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:41.930
Hurry up and close the door.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:58.730
It's pitch dark.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.140
Keep walking straight.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:03.490
- Down there?
- You'll soon... be there.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.610
Wait a minute.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.210
You haven't told us anything.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:08.250
- She's right.
- This is as far as I'm going.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.090
You'll know when you get there.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.490
Thanks. We'll do that.

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:13.010
Luffy, you idiot!

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.320
This doesn't look right.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.250
It's probably a trap!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:17.810
Don't go if you don't want to.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:20.210
That'd make me sleep better.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:21.610
We're going.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:23.770
I smell adventure.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.420
Adventure, eh?

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.290
You better not be
lying about the money.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:30.810
I'm not lying.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.650
But I'm not telling you
anything more.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:37.810
I have
the “don't go into the tunnel“ syndrome...

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.290
Give up, Usopp-

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:41.370
Our captain is ready to go already.

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:44.770
And it's true we need the money.
We have no choice.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:47.240
But I have a bad feeling about this.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.690
Is there adventure down there?

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:51.690
- Yeah.
- Wow!

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:53.730
Whatever will be will be.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:54.930
We can
think about it later.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.090
O-kay!

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.250
Let's go.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:59.530
Ready to go get money
so I can eat?

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:01.250
Is that all you think about?

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:05.810
Get out two 100 berry coins
when you reach the end.

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.490
That's the password.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:08.970
Thanks, mister.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:11.450
Let me ask you something.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:12.760
What?

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:15.250
Why did you become a pirate?

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.010
To become the pirate king.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:21.080
And out on the ocean, there's freedom,

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:22.730
treasure, and adventure.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.930
Lots of fun things!

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:29.290
I like you, kid.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:32.850
Stay alive.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:46.930
What is it?

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.090
Nothing.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:55.290
Wow, It's hot!

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:58.090
Zoro!
What are you...?

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:00.770
Who the hell are you?

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:02.490
Sanji-kun, wait.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:07.610
Zoro, get out of my way.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:11.050
Don't be alarmed.
Here, let me show you.

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:14.050
See?

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.050
WOW!
What is this place?

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:59.980
There's a ship hanging from the ceiling.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.530
Ow... that was hot.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:03.980
What is this really?

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:07.970
There were hardly any ships in the harbour.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:10.730
Hey girlie.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.810
Did you come here to place a bet?

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.730
The bookie's upstairs.

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:17.690
Bookie?

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:21.490
You're not going to
enter the race, are you?

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.290
What race?

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:27.050
Don't even think about it.
You'll never live through it.

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:30.090
Now I remember.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:33.010
It's been long since I was here before.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:34.970
What do you mean?

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:39.130
I was here before with a captain of a
pirate ship that I was on a long time ago

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:43.650
Once every few years,
there's a race.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:47.890
A race by pirates for pirates.
A “dead end“ race. Anything goes.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:48.970
Pirates?

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.050
“Ex“ pirates to be exact.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.890
This town is full of ex-pirates.

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:56.610
The goal is different each time,

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:58.450
but the race always starts in this town.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:01.610
You use an Eternal Pose to find the goal.

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.130
The rules are simple,

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:05.450
The ship to get to the goal first is the winner

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:07.210
and gets the prize money.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:10.650
You can do anything to get there.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.690
Anything to win.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.530
Yeah?!

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.890
That's easy to understand.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.410
Like what's about to happen now.

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:23.780
Sounds like a wild race...

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:27.370
But we'll be all right.

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:30.010
I'm sure Luffy wants to enter.

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:32.930
What kind of people are competing?

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:34.370
Do you know anything?

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:36.330
You're really going to enter the race?

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:40.600
Well, I suppose a third of the people
here are gonna enter anyway.

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:43.690
Wow! So many?!

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:46.210
The third favourite-to-win is down there.

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:47.730
Down there?

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.040
Those two big guys.

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:52.050
Fishermen from the Giant Tribe,
Bobby and Pogo.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.650
Cool!
Even the Giant Tribe is entering the race.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.410
Right across over there...

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:05.650
Arlong's former rival and the second
favourite Willy, killer whale merman.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.370
Even a merman!

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:13.130
Willy, Arlong's rival!

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:16.960
Hey Luffy!
We still haven't decided to enter the race.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.410
What good will...
possibly..

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:21.650
Come out of entering
something fishy like this?

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:22.730
LISTEN!

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:24.930
And how much is the prize money?

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.760
This year, it's 300 million berries.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.250
Come on, let's win this race!

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:32.130
- Yeah!
- Hey!

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:37.180
There's my signature.

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:38.970
Okay.
Now the money.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.970
- Money?
- You know what I'm talking about.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:42.850
Oh, this...

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:48.130
Very good.

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:56.250
Partia?

00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:58.250
This year's goal?

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:00.130
Yeah, good luck.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:01.970
The place is known for cyclones.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.380
Be careful.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:04.490
Thank you.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:08.970
You've got a lot of entries.

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:11.130
But there were no ships in the harbour.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:13.490
Is that YOUR ship?
The one in the harbour?

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:15.450
Oops... Were we supposed to hide it?

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:18.000
Everyone's hiding their ship
on different parts of the island.

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:20.450
What if
the marines spot you?

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:29.210
Grandpa!

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:31.370
Grandpa!
You okay?

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:34.100
I'm fine.
This is nothing.

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.970
Of course you're not fine!

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.520
You've had a fever for the past week.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.130
Don't worry about it.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:42.450
I'm not gonna die yet.

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:45.810
Come on.
We have to check the boiler.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.370
No!
You have to stay in bed.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.170
I'm fine.
Totally fine.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:50.730
Grandpa!

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:54.730
Yeah, we'll be careful.

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:59.490
But it'll be okay.
The race starts tomorrow morning.

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:02.170
You can be a little late.
No problem.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:04.130
It's a “parade start.“

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:05.410
All right.

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.330
Hey, wait a minute.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:10.050
You can place a bet, you know.

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:11.250
How about it?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.330
That's obvious.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.770
Of course
we're gonna bet on ourselves!

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:15.970
That'd be something!

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:18.890
Your odds are 350 to 1.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.250
Who's the favourite?

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:22.770
Gusparday.

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.320
General Gusparday.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:27.010
Gusparday?

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:28.090
Uh huh.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:29.730
I thought you would know.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.200
Sounds familiar
but then again not.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.940
I guess he's the favourite.
I wonder who he is.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.650
Where are the guys?

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.330
They went to the cafeteria downstairs.

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:41.530
The food here is free.

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.010
They left
as soon as they heard that.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:44.090
I see!

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:50.490
Didn't you just eat 'til you were full?

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.050
No, I was only half full.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.530
Sure, whatever.

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:54.840
Tomorrow is the race.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.650
We need stamina.

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:57.770
Uh huh!

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:59.130
You don't have to do everything he does.

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:00.930
- Really? I don't?
- Uh huh.

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:10.330
Hey, those look good.

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:11.610
Give them to me.

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:12.690
No.

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:14.970
I have to bring them to that table.

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:17.440
Don't be a jerk.
Get them something else.

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:25.770
Hey, what are you doing?

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:27.290
Hurry up and bring the food.

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:28.930
Yes. Coming.

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:31.490
Hm?!
What? What?

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:33.850
- Yo!!
- Yes, yes. Coming.

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:36.450
This place is great!

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:38.690
The food keeps coming and coming.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:41.460
Your stomach must be bottomless.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:54.050
What was that for?

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:55.930
What was that for?!

00:18:56.020 --> 00:18:57.610
What was that for?!

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.130
What was that for?
What?

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:00.690
That's what I'd like to know!

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.130
You're not making any sense!

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:03.330
Shut up!

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:06.130
He was stealing my food.

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:10.970
Just because he can stretch his arms.
Stretch...his arms...?

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:13.170
HIS ARMS WERE STRETCHED!!!

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:14.250
You are slow

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:16.210
Yeah.

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:18.690
You're asking for it.

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.050
You ate the Devil's Fruit?

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:23.170
So what if I did?

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.850
Hey, hey. hey--

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:28.250
You stole all our food.
We saw you.

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:30.690
Don't you know who we are?

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.450
We're with General Gusparday.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:39.970
Don't think you can talk back to us
and get away with it.

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:43.740
You're history even before the race starts...

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:47.730
What? You 're gonna apologize?
It's a little too late for that.

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:49.090
Hey!

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:50.770
You're still fighting with me

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:56.490
Shut up, punk

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.170
What are you looking at?

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:01.610
That doesn't work.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.220
Because I'm rubber.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:12.450
Hey! What was THAT for?!

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:13.650
You surprised me.

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:16.380
Normally people would be
more than surprised...

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:18.370
What the hell are you?!

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:20.530
Me? I ate the Gum Gum Fruit.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:23.330
So now I'm rubber!

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:27.370
<i>Gum-Gum...</i>

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:28.680
<i>Pistol!!!</i>

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:39.010
How's that?

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:40.520
Monster!

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:42.170
He ate the Devil's Fruit?!

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.850
Like General Gusparday.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:44.930
Hey, wait.

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:46.010
We should just leave him alone.

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:47.130
Idiot!

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:49.170
Don't be such a wimp.
He's just a kid.

00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:51.850
Everyone, Get him!!

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:52.930
Arrrhh!

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:38.130
Oh no...! They're coming!

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:39.540
- Go get 'em, Zoro!
- You...

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:47.810
Don't make me work
any harder than I have to.

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:49.690
Who is this?

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:51.130
Way to go!

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:52.210
I told you not to move!

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:03.210
We're gonna get you!

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:07.760
Lousy fighters.
So annoying.

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:09.290
Let's stop this...

00:22:09.380 --> 00:22:10.450
You!

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:11.530
Dead meat!

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:13.090
Stand up!

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:14.930
Wow! Cool!

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:16.730
Luffy!
What are you doing?

00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:18.140
Nothing. It's a fight.

00:22:18.220 --> 00:22:20.210
Oh, okay. Just don't get lost.

00:22:20.300 --> 00:22:22.940
- Okay.
- This is the end.

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:29.090
- Stop! We got you...
- Wait!

00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:31.610
Idiots! The rope's gonna rip!

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:35.050
You think
you can scare a pirate like that?

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:36.690
All right...

00:22:48.740 --> 00:22:50.450
You still want more?

00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:52.930
That was excellent.

00:22:53.420 --> 00:22:56.250
You're really good.
It was just fun watching you.

00:22:56.340 --> 00:22:57.850
Oh, thanks.

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:02.450
I never thought I'd come face to face
with a 30 million-berry bounty.

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:04.370
What's your name?

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:05.680
Me?

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:06.810
I'm Sh...

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:08.040
Hey, hey. hey--

00:23:08.140 --> 00:23:10.370
You think
you can just ignore me?

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:11.450
Haven't you had enough?

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:12.570
It's not over!

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:15.650
30 million berries?
Don't even flatter yourself.

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:19.690
Our boss is 95 million!!
He's the big deal!

00:23:19.780 --> 00:23:20.970
Wow, cool!

00:23:21.060 --> 00:23:22.410
He's more than Crocodile!

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:25.970
And you think his crewman
is gonna let you get away with this?

00:23:26.060 --> 00:23:27.690
That could happen.

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:28.920
Of course not!

00:23:35.340 --> 00:23:36.370
See ya.

00:23:38.340 --> 00:23:40.130
He is really light...

00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:41.930
But this is not
the time to be impressed

00:23:49.340 --> 00:23:51.090
You saved him?

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:52.370
You're strange...

00:23:52.460 --> 00:23:53.490
I was passing by.

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:54.940
So?
Shall we continue?

00:23:55.020 --> 00:23:56.130
Oh, yeah.
That's right.

00:23:56.780 --> 00:23:58.000
Okay, you ready?

00:23:58.220 --> 00:23:59.440
Um, yeah...

00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:01.010
But it seems
he wants another go.

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:03.050
You!

00:24:03.140 --> 00:24:04.250
Forget it, man.

00:24:05.180 --> 00:24:07.050
What's the ruckus?

00:24:31.940 --> 00:24:34.650
General Gusparday?

00:24:34.740 --> 00:24:36.090
Why are you here?

00:24:36.180 --> 00:24:37.170
Gusparday?

00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:39.640
Aren't I allowed to be here?

00:24:39.740 --> 00:24:40.930
Of course you are!

00:24:41.340 --> 00:24:44.770
I just thought
you were drinking on the ship today.

00:24:45.420 --> 00:24:48.090
I don't need
your permission to come here.

00:24:48.180 --> 00:24:50.530
Of course you don't!
lam so sorry.

00:24:50.660 --> 00:24:52.490
Please enjoy yourself.

00:24:52.620 --> 00:24:54.290
Let me ask you something.

00:24:54.380 --> 00:24:55.370
Yes, sir.

00:24:56.660 --> 00:24:57.850
Who are you?

00:24:58.420 --> 00:25:00.530
Excuse me? Who am I?

00:25:00.660 --> 00:25:01.800
Are you serious?

00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:03.930
- General... it's me...
- I don't know you.

00:25:05.100 --> 00:25:08.850
I don't know a pirate
who gets beat up by some jerk

00:25:08.940 --> 00:25:11.250
I don't need anyone like that
on my crew!

00:25:11.460 --> 00:25:13.250
Um, this is... you know...

00:25:13.460 --> 00:25:14.890
Please forgive me.

00:25:15.020 --> 00:25:16.090
The fight is not over yet.

00:25:23.540 --> 00:25:25.450
What's going on?

00:25:25.540 --> 00:25:27.050
That was cold.

00:25:28.740 --> 00:25:29.810
Useless fool.

00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:35.290
What was that?

00:25:35.380 --> 00:25:37.050
Hey, isn't that Gusparday?

00:25:37.140 --> 00:25:38.210
The General...

00:25:39.740 --> 00:25:41.530
You were getting pretty wild there.

00:25:41.660 --> 00:25:42.690
Who are you?

00:25:42.780 --> 00:25:45.010
My name is Shryer...

00:25:45.100 --> 00:25:48.490
a bounty hunter.
The jerk you don't know.

00:25:49.260 --> 00:25:51.050
- What? Shryer?
- Is he real?

00:25:51.140 --> 00:25:54.010
Shryer the Pirate Hunter?
I hear about him all the time

00:25:55.420 --> 00:25:58.250
Shryer Bascudo?

00:26:00.060 --> 00:26:02.210
You're a bounty hunter, huh?

00:26:02.300 --> 00:26:03.330
I suppose.

00:26:03.420 --> 00:26:05.170
A rather famous one.

00:26:05.260 --> 00:26:07.250
I've seen you somewhere too.

00:26:07.860 --> 00:26:12.090
You don't look like 30 million,
but you did okay.

00:26:12.180 --> 00:26:13.210
I like that.

00:26:13.540 --> 00:26:14.530
You two...

00:26:14.860 --> 00:26:17.210
Why don't you come work for me?

00:26:17.580 --> 00:26:20.810
I work for the other side.
I'm supposed to bring you in.

00:26:21.340 --> 00:26:23.450
I used to be a marine myself.

00:26:23.580 --> 00:26:26.090
I don't mind
as long as you have the skill and guts.

00:26:26.180 --> 00:26:28.090
I like a strong crew.

00:26:28.300 --> 00:26:30.410
That's a bold remark.

00:26:30.500 --> 00:26:31.930
So what do you think?

00:26:32.020 --> 00:26:33.050
No.

00:26:33.660 --> 00:26:35.730
He reeks of trash.

00:26:43.300 --> 00:26:44.370
My hat!

00:26:45.820 --> 00:26:47.930
I like spunk...

00:26:48.020 --> 00:26:50.170
but don't be a smart ass.

00:26:50.340 --> 00:26:51.850
You'll lose your life.

00:26:52.980 --> 00:26:54.370
Do whatever you like...

00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:59.650
But, what can you do
when you're dead?

00:27:00.340 --> 00:27:02.330
Come see me on the ship
when you change your mind.

00:27:04.020 --> 00:27:05.240
Needles.

00:27:05.340 --> 00:27:07.770
We'll win the race anyway,
let him go.

00:27:13.660 --> 00:27:14.690
Don't...

00:27:14.780 --> 00:27:16.170
step on that!!

00:27:17.380 --> 00:27:18.450
Get away!

00:27:19.260 --> 00:27:20.450
Don't touch it!

00:27:20.940 --> 00:27:21.970
This is my treasure.

00:27:22.580 --> 00:27:23.800
That hat is your treasure?

00:27:23.900 --> 00:27:27.600
It's real precious to me.
A hat that I'm keeping for Shanks.

00:27:27.700 --> 00:27:29.810
Shanks?
That great pirate?

00:27:30.220 --> 00:27:33.770
- Yeah.
- You're not just a normal pirate.

00:27:33.860 --> 00:27:36.130
Yeah,
I'm just a regular pirate...

00:27:36.220 --> 00:27:39.010
I'm looking for
the legendary treasure, One Piece.

00:27:39.100 --> 00:27:42.370
But I guess if I become the Pirate King...

00:27:42.460 --> 00:27:43.730
I won't be a normal pirate anymore.

00:27:46.020 --> 00:27:48.170
You talk big, kid.

00:27:48.820 --> 00:27:51.970
You know what you're in for
by saying that around here?

00:27:52.300 --> 00:27:55.210
No. I decided I'm gonna be the Pirate King.

00:27:55.780 --> 00:27:57.930
If I have to die fighting for it, then...

00:27:58.020 --> 00:27:59.210
be it.

00:28:02.580 --> 00:28:04.850
Luffy, the big liar.

00:28:08.300 --> 00:28:09.410
Hm?

00:28:13.860 --> 00:28:16.370
I don't feel like
fighting you anymore.

00:28:16.460 --> 00:28:18.450
Let's continue this
some other time.

00:28:18.580 --> 00:28:19.650
Okay?

00:28:19.740 --> 00:28:20.770
Sure.

00:28:22.660 --> 00:28:24.850
I'm gonna go for
your head the next time.

00:28:32.020 --> 00:28:33.650
Come on, PLEASE!

00:28:34.020 --> 00:28:35.490
Wait!

00:28:36.180 --> 00:28:37.320
Shut up!

00:28:37.420 --> 00:28:38.890
I've had enough of you.

00:28:43.820 --> 00:28:45.730
Grandpa needs a doctor!

00:28:45.820 --> 00:28:47.610
Or else he'll die!

00:28:47.940 --> 00:28:49.570
I don't give a damn.
Let go!

00:28:49.940 --> 00:28:51.730
We're mates on the same crew!

00:28:51.820 --> 00:28:52.810
How can you be so cruel?

00:28:52.900 --> 00:28:53.890
Mates?

00:28:53.980 --> 00:28:55.810
That old geezer is not my mate.

00:28:56.140 --> 00:28:57.170
How can you say that?

00:28:57.260 --> 00:28:58.850
If Grandpa wasn't
taking care of the boiler...

00:28:58.940 --> 00:29:00.490
What's going on?

00:29:01.060 --> 00:29:02.570
What's all the shouting?

00:29:05.020 --> 00:29:06.210
General Gusparday.

00:29:06.300 --> 00:29:07.290
Hey! Come back!

00:29:08.180 --> 00:29:09.810
You have to help Grandpa.

00:29:09.900 --> 00:29:11.490
Please help
Grandpa Biera.

00:29:11.620 --> 00:29:12.730
You idiot.
Stop that.

00:29:12.820 --> 00:29:14.010
His fever is getting worse.

00:29:14.100 --> 00:29:16.170
He can't even get up from bed.

00:29:16.260 --> 00:29:17.400
He needs medicine!

00:29:17.500 --> 00:29:19.170
Don't be a pest!

00:29:19.260 --> 00:29:20.290
Please!

00:29:20.380 --> 00:29:22.170
General Gusparday!

00:29:22.900 --> 00:29:23.890
Badger?

00:29:23.980 --> 00:29:26.090
The old man
in the boiler room is the Old Mole.

00:29:26.180 --> 00:29:28.370
So his assistant is the
“Badger?

00:29:28.980 --> 00:29:31.410
So what's wrong with
the Old Mole?

00:29:31.500 --> 00:29:32.720
He's sick.

00:29:32.820 --> 00:29:35.050
But he's old anyway.
He's not gonna make it.

00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:36.970
- Yes, he will!
- As long as he gets some medicine!

00:29:37.060 --> 00:29:38.810
It's a waste of time.

00:29:38.900 --> 00:29:40.010
Anyway, he's...

00:29:40.100 --> 00:29:41.810
I promise I'll work my butt off!

00:29:41.900 --> 00:29:42.890
I'll do anything!

00:29:42.980 --> 00:29:46.290
- So please, I beg you.
- Stop talking like that, kid.

00:29:52.180 --> 00:29:54.290
Hm? You crying?

00:29:55.020 --> 00:29:56.410
Get lost!

00:30:00.660 --> 00:30:01.930
I don't need your help!

00:30:04.620 --> 00:30:06.890
That's...
What are you doing?!

00:30:06.980 --> 00:30:09.570
I'll go get help by myself.
Just let me borrow this gun!

00:30:09.900 --> 00:30:11.690
- You little punk!
- Wait.

00:30:11.780 --> 00:30:14.290
That's not a toy for kids.

00:30:14.380 --> 00:30:16.370
I'm gonna use this
to kill a pirate.

00:30:16.460 --> 00:30:18.610
I'll use the bounty
to buy medicine!

00:30:19.020 --> 00:30:20.010
Stop talking nonsense

00:30:20.100 --> 00:30:22.480
No one's stupid enough
to get killed by a kid!

00:30:22.620 --> 00:30:23.730
I said I can do it.

00:30:23.820 --> 00:30:24.850
That's enough.

00:30:24.940 --> 00:30:26.130
- Let him try.
- Huh?

00:30:26.220 --> 00:30:31.450
Tonight, there're loads of big-talking rookies
and fools with muscles but no brain.

00:30:31.860 --> 00:30:35.490
If you can pull it off,
you are officially my crew

00:30:35.620 --> 00:30:36.690
Really?

00:30:36.780 --> 00:30:40.660
Even a fool's head
will be worth something.

00:30:48.060 --> 00:30:51.050
Get better, Grandpa.
I'll get you something decent to eat

00:31:13.620 --> 00:31:15.490
Hey...
Are you okay?

00:31:15.620 --> 00:31:17.130
I'm all right.

00:31:41.060 --> 00:31:42.850
It's that mountain for sure.

00:31:43.180 --> 00:31:44.370
What is it, Nami?

00:31:44.900 --> 00:31:48.090
This Eternal Pose is
pointing to that mountain over there.

00:31:48.420 --> 00:31:50.410
The starting point is on the other side?

00:31:51.820 --> 00:31:54.850
No,
The bookie said we start in this town

00:31:55.060 --> 00:31:58.250
None of the other ships are here.
Did they already start without us?

00:31:58.340 --> 00:32:00.010
- Zoro always get left behind.
- Shut up!

00:32:00.100 --> 00:32:01.730
What's going on?

00:32:03.180 --> 00:32:05.170
This is the starting point.

00:32:05.260 --> 00:32:07.900
This island has a lot of tributaries...

00:32:07.980 --> 00:32:10.690
and they all merge
in that mountain in front of us.

00:32:10.780 --> 00:32:12.210
You mean...

00:32:12.300 --> 00:32:13.330
that mountain?

00:32:13.420 --> 00:32:16.250
Everyone's probably
standing by in the other tributaries.

00:32:16.340 --> 00:32:18.930
The starting point is
that mountain's peak.

00:32:19.020 --> 00:32:20.610
What? Wait a sec.

00:32:20.700 --> 00:32:21.970
You mean,
we have to go UP a mountain?

00:32:22.060 --> 00:32:23.050
Uh huh.

00:32:23.140 --> 00:32:25.250
But we've already done that
on Reverse Mountain.

00:32:25.340 --> 00:32:28.690
Yeah, but it had a huge current...

00:32:28.780 --> 00:32:30.000
There's one here too.

00:32:30.300 --> 00:32:34.180
Once every few years, the current reverses
and the wind blows upstream.

00:32:34.260 --> 00:32:35.690
We have to use them.

00:32:35.780 --> 00:32:38.240
You're so knowledgeable,
Robin-chan.

00:32:38.420 --> 00:32:40.650
Well, I can see that in theory but...

00:32:40.740 --> 00:32:42.170
In other words,
it's a Mystery Start.

00:32:42.260 --> 00:32:43.400
No, it isn't.

00:32:43.900 --> 00:32:45.690
Are we gonna be okay?

00:32:45.780 --> 00:32:49.010
Remember that time,
we almost wrecked the ship.

00:32:49.180 --> 00:32:50.650
We're gonna be okay.

00:32:50.740 --> 00:32:52.370
We'll find a way!

00:32:58.180 --> 00:32:59.210
The wind!

00:32:59.300 --> 00:33:01.090
Luffy, hurry up and reinforce the yard!

00:33:01.180 --> 00:33:02.450
Usopp, the rudder!

00:33:02.580 --> 00:33:04.170
Chopper, to the stern!

00:33:04.260 --> 00:33:06.970
Sanji-kun and Zoro,
watch the shrouds on both sides!

00:33:25.340 --> 00:33:26.330
Here it comes.

00:33:41.060 --> 00:33:43.290
Not another tunnel!

00:33:48.820 --> 00:33:52.520
All right! Let's go!

00:34:13.300 --> 00:34:14.570
I see.

00:34:14.660 --> 00:34:16.730
This is the Parade Start.

00:34:19.780 --> 00:34:20.920
Hey, hey, hey!

00:34:21.020 --> 00:34:23.850
I think we're one of the favourites!

00:34:23.940 --> 00:34:25.570
Let's win this race!

00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:27.930
You guys, don't do anything
to mess up the odds!

00:34:28.020 --> 00:34:29.890
Our money's on the favourite!

00:34:29.980 --> 00:34:32.050
We'll kill you if you get in his way!

00:34:32.300 --> 00:34:34.210
This was to be expected.

00:34:34.300 --> 00:34:35.890
Who's Gusparday?

00:34:35.980 --> 00:34:37.850
You're interested?
It's not like you.

00:34:37.940 --> 00:34:40.050
You were
checking up on him 'til late last night.

00:34:40.220 --> 00:34:41.210
Wow.

00:34:41.300 --> 00:34:42.650
We're really going up the mountain!

00:34:42.740 --> 00:34:43.810
This is nothing!

00:34:44.180 --> 00:34:47.810
Wanna hear how, thanks to me,
we were able to go up Reverse Mountain?

00:34:47.900 --> 00:34:48.890
YES!

00:34:51.900 --> 00:34:53.570
There they are. The other ships.

00:34:55.020 --> 00:34:56.410
And this side too.

00:35:03.300 --> 00:35:05.570
Mm?
Look at that. A huge one.

00:35:07.620 --> 00:35:08.940
A steamboat.

00:35:09.460 --> 00:35:10.970
I've never seen one before.

00:35:11.300 --> 00:35:14.770
That's the favourite of this race.
Gusparday's ship, the Salamander.

00:35:14.860 --> 00:35:15.970
So that's it...

00:35:16.140 --> 00:35:17.930
What's that on the flag?

00:35:18.020 --> 00:35:20.250
A cross over
the mark of the marines?

00:35:20.340 --> 00:35:23.250
Yup.
He used to be a marine.

00:35:23.340 --> 00:35:27.090
He hijacked his own ship
and became a pirate.

00:35:27.180 --> 00:35:29.450
There's a 95 million-berry bounty
on his head.

00:35:29.580 --> 00:35:30.690
Ninety five.

00:35:30.780 --> 00:35:32.690
What I? He's a biggie.

00:35:32.780 --> 00:35:33.810
Yeah.

00:35:33.900 --> 00:35:36.090
He's very skilled
We have to keep an eye on him.

00:35:36.300 --> 00:35:38.210
And he's also eaten the Devil's Fruit.

00:35:39.620 --> 00:35:41.730
His nickname is the General.

00:35:41.820 --> 00:35:43.730
<i>Bu“ doth 'near
too mam; good 'Mugs about Mm.</i>

00:35:43.820 --> 00:35:45.250
Good things.

00:35:45.340 --> 00:35:46.970
Well, he's a pirate.
What do you expect?

00:35:47.060 --> 00:35:48.730
Who cares?
It doesn't matter.

00:35:48.820 --> 00:35:49.810
Luffy?

00:35:49.900 --> 00:35:51.850
I don't like him.

00:36:03.660 --> 00:36:06.120
What is that shabby little ship you're on?

00:36:06.220 --> 00:36:09.290
You think you can survive
the Grand Fall on her?!

00:36:09.580 --> 00:36:11.650
That's Bigalo the Choker.

00:36:15.660 --> 00:36:17.010
That's Willy!

00:36:18.180 --> 00:36:20.130
And the Giant Tribe!

00:36:29.820 --> 00:36:33.130
It's getting steeper and steeper!

00:36:34.380 --> 00:36:36.290
Not a problem.

00:36:49.820 --> 00:36:51.610
I'll resign myself to fate.

00:37:40.580 --> 00:37:42.210
So that was the Grand Fall...

00:37:42.300 --> 00:37:44.940
Come on, Navigator-san!
We have no time to waste.

00:37:56.100 --> 00:37:57.690
What are they doing?

00:37:57.780 --> 00:37:59.690
The race has started.

00:37:59.780 --> 00:38:01.690
Anything goes.

00:38:01.780 --> 00:38:04.160
Usopp,
go to the stern and stand guard!

00:38:04.260 --> 00:38:05.400
Me?!

00:38:07.460 --> 00:38:08.890
Get out of my way!

00:38:08.980 --> 00:38:10.410
They' re here already.

00:38:11.220 --> 00:38:13.860
Okay, okay!
I'll DO it...

00:38:13.940 --> 00:38:14.930
Fine!

00:38:15.780 --> 00:38:16.850
THERE!

00:38:21.380 --> 00:38:22.650
Yeah!

00:38:22.740 --> 00:38:25.120
This is what a REAL man can do.

00:38:46.500 --> 00:38:47.720
Look at 'em!

00:38:48.620 --> 00:38:51.080
They're having so much fun!

00:39:03.860 --> 00:39:06.930
Bobby, we won't make the turn
with this speed!

00:39:07.020 --> 00:39:09.170
Then we'll just have to
speed up some more!

00:39:09.420 --> 00:39:10.890
You're right!

00:39:24.180 --> 00:39:25.850
Oh no.
We don't have enough distance!

00:39:26.100 --> 00:39:27.130
What?

00:39:30.220 --> 00:39:31.650
Chopper!
Turn the rudder!

00:39:33.380 --> 00:39:35.090
But it's not working!

00:39:35.180 --> 00:39:36.650
We're gonna crash!

00:39:36.860 --> 00:39:38.970
Hey!
We're going off course!

00:39:39.060 --> 00:39:40.730
You think
we can kick her to cushion her?

00:39:40.820 --> 00:39:42.140
Of course not!

00:39:42.220 --> 00:39:43.650
Oh! A cushion!

00:39:44.100 --> 00:39:45.090
Luffy!

00:39:45.740 --> 00:39:47.930
<i>Gum-Gum...</i>

00:39:50.140 --> 00:39:51.460
<i>BALLOON!!!!!</i>

00:39:57.940 --> 00:39:58.930
Luffy!

00:40:00.420 --> 00:40:01.450
There!

00:40:04.380 --> 00:40:05.450
But...

00:40:05.580 --> 00:40:07.410
NOW what?!

00:40:08.660 --> 00:40:09.730
Grand Fleur...!

00:40:19.300 --> 00:40:22.650
Good going, Robin!

00:40:30.180 --> 00:40:33.250
Every time it amazes me...

00:40:33.340 --> 00:40:35.900
how we're still alive.

00:40:36.580 --> 00:40:37.650
Thanks Robin.

00:40:37.740 --> 00:40:39.090
Just as I had planned.

00:40:39.180 --> 00:40:40.210
Liar!

00:40:40.300 --> 00:40:41.490
Okay, now the race.

00:40:41.580 --> 00:40:42.570
Let's enjoy it!

00:40:42.660 --> 00:40:45.300
Yeah!
This is gonna be so much fun!!

00:40:45.700 --> 00:40:47.370
We're one of the last ones...

00:40:47.460 --> 00:40:49.130
but we'll catch up.

00:40:49.340 --> 00:40:51.050
This is why I love being a pirate!

00:40:51.140 --> 00:40:53.370
300 million berries...
300 million berries...

00:40:53.700 --> 00:40:54.920
I've got the

00:40:55.020 --> 00:40:56.160
“...don't leave the island“ syndrome...

00:40:56.820 --> 00:40:58.290
Yeah!

00:41:07.060 --> 00:41:08.970
....

00:41:09.620 --> 00:41:11.970
It's all because of
that bounty hunter and the kid...

00:41:12.060 --> 00:41:13.890
I'm demoted
to be a boiler man

00:41:13.980 --> 00:41:15.200
l hate this...

00:41:17.580 --> 00:41:19.090
This is the worst!

00:41:19.180 --> 00:41:22.170
Who said you could feed the boiler!

00:41:22.260 --> 00:41:23.650
Shut up!

00:41:23.740 --> 00:41:24.810
It's not like we WANT to be down here.

00:41:24.900 --> 00:41:27.410
This is no work for an amateur.

00:41:27.500 --> 00:41:29.250
That's fine by me.

00:41:29.340 --> 00:41:30.850
Where's Badger?

00:41:31.020 --> 00:41:32.050
Badger?

00:41:32.140 --> 00:41:33.280
My assistant.

00:41:33.380 --> 00:41:35.840
Oh, Yeah... I heard.

00:41:35.940 --> 00:41:38.850
He went to kill a pirate.

00:41:38.940 --> 00:41:39.970
What?!

00:41:43.340 --> 00:41:45.450
Where are all the other ships?

00:41:45.580 --> 00:41:49.170
We're all sailing on different courses.

00:41:49.260 --> 00:41:51.130
I'll go make lunch.

00:41:51.220 --> 00:41:52.250
Thank you!

00:41:52.340 --> 00:41:54.370
Go check for any damages,
Zoro.

00:41:54.460 --> 00:41:55.810
Why just me?!

00:41:57.180 --> 00:41:59.850
She's such a slave driver.

00:42:01.020 --> 00:42:03.660
Any holes...?

00:42:06.140 --> 00:42:08.810
Nope, it looks fine in here...

00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:19.370
You chose the wrong ship
to get a free ride.

00:42:19.460 --> 00:42:21.130
This is a pirate ship.

00:42:30.100 --> 00:42:31.730
A KID?!

00:42:32.740 --> 00:42:34.570
You are so cruel.

00:42:34.660 --> 00:42:36.610
How can you do this to a child?

00:42:36.700 --> 00:42:38.930
I couldn't help it.
He had a gun.

00:42:39.020 --> 00:42:40.810
Zoro, you meanie!!

00:42:40.900 --> 00:42:42.010
You guys...

00:42:42.340 --> 00:42:43.970
Lunch is almost ready.

00:42:44.060 --> 00:42:45.280
Everybody, go wash your hands.

00:42:45.380 --> 00:42:47.130
Yes sir!

00:42:48.220 --> 00:42:49.170
Look. He's waking up.

00:42:51.820 --> 00:42:52.930
A talking deer.

00:42:53.020 --> 00:42:54.370
I'm not a deer!
I'm a reindeer!

00:42:54.460 --> 00:42:56.650
- That's even weirder.
- Shut up, you!

00:42:57.020 --> 00:42:59.170
Don't call him a monster.

00:42:59.460 --> 00:43:01.570
He's a very good doctor.

00:43:01.660 --> 00:43:04.090
Just not very good at
expressing himself.

00:43:04.180 --> 00:43:05.570
Oh, you...

00:43:05.660 --> 00:43:07.690
Don't butter me up like that...

00:43:07.780 --> 00:43:09.130
- ...you fool!
- See?

00:43:09.220 --> 00:43:10.690
Like that.

00:43:11.460 --> 00:43:12.930
Are you looking for this?

00:43:14.140 --> 00:43:17.050
You could get yourself killed...

00:43:17.140 --> 00:43:19.290
trying to smuggle yourself into a pirate ship.

00:43:19.780 --> 00:43:20.970
Why are you here?

00:43:21.060 --> 00:43:22.450
Who do you work for?

00:43:24.460 --> 00:43:25.890
Take it easy.

00:43:25.980 --> 00:43:27.810
The kid isn't feeling too well.

00:43:27.900 --> 00:43:29.690
We can do this later.
And by the way...

00:43:29.780 --> 00:43:31.330
To kill you.

00:43:31.420 --> 00:43:34.210
To kill you and to get the bounty!

00:43:34.300 --> 00:43:35.290
Money, huh.

00:43:35.380 --> 00:43:36.570
That's pretty straightforward.

00:43:36.660 --> 00:43:38.730
But there're other pirates.

00:43:38.820 --> 00:43:40.040
Why this ship?

00:43:40.940 --> 00:43:42.770
That's obvious...

00:43:42.860 --> 00:43:46.810
We're the famous
"Straw Hat Pirates," right?

00:43:47.060 --> 00:43:48.090
Never heard of you guys!

00:43:48.180 --> 00:43:50.170
This ship just looked the weakest.

00:43:50.260 --> 00:43:51.450
Laugh, this is funny.

00:43:52.060 --> 00:43:54.130
Don't laugh! I'm serious!

00:43:54.220 --> 00:43:55.810
Stop it.
You're hurt.

00:43:55.900 --> 00:43:57.040
Stay away!

00:43:57.620 --> 00:44:00.570
A pirate's life is
always in danger from bounty hunters.

00:44:01.420 --> 00:44:05.050
If you're just half-hearted about this,
you'll never get me.

00:44:09.740 --> 00:44:11.010
Show us what you've got.

00:44:11.100 --> 00:44:13.930
Or... Are you all talk?

00:44:14.860 --> 00:44:15.930
O-Of course not!!

00:44:16.020 --> 00:44:19.450
Take... THIS!

00:44:26.460 --> 00:44:29.650
What was that?!

00:44:30.860 --> 00:44:32.930
The...the Devil's Fruit?

00:44:34.300 --> 00:44:36.050
That's right.
You've never seen this?

00:44:36.140 --> 00:44:37.730
I've never been off the ship.

00:44:37.820 --> 00:44:39.810
It's a real spooky fruit.

00:44:39.900 --> 00:44:41.850
If you eat one,
you become unable to swim..

00:44:41.940 --> 00:44:44.090
But instead, you get superhuman abilities.

00:44:44.180 --> 00:44:47.960
On this ship,
Robin and that Chopper also ate one.

00:44:48.060 --> 00:44:49.050
This deer?

00:44:49.140 --> 00:44:50.610
REINDEER!

00:44:51.580 --> 00:44:52.800
Like that.

00:44:54.060 --> 00:44:55.090
Kill me...

00:44:55.900 --> 00:44:57.090
Just kill me.

00:44:57.180 --> 00:44:58.500
Let's finish this right now.

00:44:58.940 --> 00:45:00.260
That's pretty gutsy of you.

00:45:00.340 --> 00:45:01.890
But

00:45:01.980 --> 00:45:04.490
don't take life too lightly.

00:45:04.900 --> 00:45:07.010
I don't want a pirate preaching at me.

00:45:07.100 --> 00:45:08.490
Who cares?

00:45:08.620 --> 00:45:10.690
What's the use of living
when there's no hope?

00:45:10.780 --> 00:45:13.690
Life is not worth living!!

00:45:14.940 --> 00:45:16.850
Zoro. Let me borrow your sword.

00:45:17.740 --> 00:45:19.010
Don't step over me.

00:45:19.460 --> 00:45:21.650
Stop talking like
you know what you're talking about.

00:45:22.260 --> 00:45:24.720
If that's what you want,
then that's what you'll get.

00:45:24.820 --> 00:45:26.570
- Don't, Nami!
- Stay out of it!

00:45:26.660 --> 00:45:28.610
Things like this
really piss me off.

00:45:28.700 --> 00:45:30.170
Life is not worth living?

00:45:30.580 --> 00:45:32.370
You're at least still alive!

00:45:32.460 --> 00:45:34.090
Don't give me that crap!

00:45:34.300 --> 00:45:35.330
That's enough.

00:45:35.420 --> 00:45:37.880
I'm sure he understands.

00:45:38.860 --> 00:45:40.330
You guys, don't just sit there!

00:45:40.580 --> 00:45:41.720
Lunch is ready!

00:45:41.820 --> 00:45:43.810
Sanji!
What kind of life have you been living?

00:45:43.900 --> 00:45:46.250
<i>Let's eat!</i>

00:45:46.340 --> 00:45:50.890
I'll cut your naïve ideas
out of you!!

00:45:56.220 --> 00:46:00.210
Grandpa, you should have never saved me.
I should have just died.

00:46:00.300 --> 00:46:02.490
Don't talk like that.

00:46:02.620 --> 00:46:04.690
You're gonna be happy one day.

00:46:05.060 --> 00:46:06.730
I'll NEVER be happy.

00:46:07.260 --> 00:46:10.050
Shut up and get to work
if you don't want me to kill you!

00:46:12.140 --> 00:46:15.090
It was so nice just a while ago.

00:46:15.780 --> 00:46:18.650
The weather on Grand Line is
really unpredictable.

00:46:18.740 --> 00:46:22.570
Our doctor's worried that
you might catch a cold.

00:46:25.380 --> 00:46:29.610
Nami-san's parents were killed by a pirate
when she was still a kid.

00:46:29.700 --> 00:46:34.050
That pirate used her
like a rag until just recently.

00:46:34.140 --> 00:46:36.780
She said those 8 years were like hell.

00:46:37.780 --> 00:46:41.330
And that reindeer,
he's also had a tough life.

00:46:41.420 --> 00:46:42.810
The others too.

00:46:42.900 --> 00:46:45.810
We're all alike in many ways.

00:46:46.220 --> 00:46:48.090
When you try to live life...

00:46:48.180 --> 00:46:51.290
it could be really hard on you.

00:46:51.980 --> 00:46:56.530
But still, there's always a tomorrow.

00:47:01.340 --> 00:47:03.650
You might not understand yet.

00:47:06.180 --> 00:47:07.930
What was that?

00:47:08.020 --> 00:47:09.650
Why are you so nice?

00:47:11.140 --> 00:47:12.650
I wonder why too.

00:47:16.500 --> 00:47:18.770
That's the entry list,
isn't it?

00:47:20.580 --> 00:47:22.130
Who cares?

00:47:23.260 --> 00:47:25.610
I won't be needing it.

00:47:32.580 --> 00:47:34.930
We're going way off course.

00:47:35.020 --> 00:47:36.290
Why aren't you doing anything?

00:47:38.300 --> 00:47:39.930
It's okay.

00:47:40.020 --> 00:47:42.170
This is just a game.

00:47:42.940 --> 00:47:45.450
A little game to kill time.

00:47:46.380 --> 00:47:48.130
General Gusparday!

00:47:48.740 --> 00:47:50.890
There's a ship on our tail.

00:47:50.980 --> 00:47:52.570
- Which one?
- Willy.

00:47:52.660 --> 00:47:53.650
Merman Willy.

00:47:55.740 --> 00:47:58.090
Aha, one of the favourites.

00:47:59.460 --> 00:48:02.100
Why are you heading that way,
Gusparday?

00:48:02.180 --> 00:48:03.850
You're up to something.

00:48:03.940 --> 00:48:06.730
You didn't think
you could fool me, did you?

00:48:06.820 --> 00:48:08.890
He's totally game.

00:48:10.420 --> 00:48:12.170
- Everybody, get ready to attack!
- What?!

00:48:13.100 --> 00:48:15.210
We got ourselves a playmate.

00:48:15.300 --> 00:48:16.620
Yes, sir.

00:48:17.860 --> 00:48:21.330
But it seems
I won't get my turn this time.

00:48:24.780 --> 00:48:28.480
You little punks are
still in the race, huh?

00:48:29.260 --> 00:48:30.290
Who's that?

00:48:30.380 --> 00:48:31.600
He better shut up.

00:48:31.700 --> 00:48:32.690
It's him.

00:48:32.780 --> 00:48:34.000
From the starting point.

00:48:34.100 --> 00:48:35.130
Bigalo, right?

00:48:35.220 --> 00:48:37.210
I thought...

00:48:37.300 --> 00:48:38.290
we were the last one.

00:48:38.380 --> 00:48:39.600
That means they are the last...

00:48:39.700 --> 00:48:41.020
What did you say?

00:48:41.300 --> 00:48:42.930
He's mad 'cuz it's the truth!

00:48:43.020 --> 00:48:44.160
You guys are going down!

00:48:44.980 --> 00:48:46.050
It's a hit?

00:48:46.140 --> 00:48:47.730
Good job, Usopp!

00:48:47.820 --> 00:48:49.490
What did I tell ya?

00:48:51.060 --> 00:48:52.610
All right, go get 'em,
you guys!

00:48:52.700 --> 00:48:54.570
- You!
- Okay then...

00:48:54.660 --> 00:48:56.930
Wait a second.
We'll handle this.

00:48:57.020 --> 00:48:58.490
Sit back and watch.

00:49:03.620 --> 00:49:06.330
We're not mad at you,
but we do fight back.

00:49:06.700 --> 00:49:09.690
I still have to
make dinner after this.

00:49:11.140 --> 00:49:13.010
We will finish this
in one minute

00:49:16.620 --> 00:49:19.290
Let's go!

00:49:24.940 --> 00:49:27.050
They're so strong!

00:49:30.380 --> 00:49:31.410
What was that?

00:49:31.500 --> 00:49:32.490
I dunno...

00:49:40.300 --> 00:49:42.680
Sea monsters!

00:49:42.780 --> 00:49:44.570
Huge ones too!

00:49:44.660 --> 00:49:46.130
They're gonna eat us!

00:49:48.940 --> 00:49:50.330
Stay calm!

00:49:50.460 --> 00:49:51.650
Hey, Wait.

00:49:51.740 --> 00:49:53.410
Grab it!

00:49:54.780 --> 00:49:56.690
Where are you aiming?!

00:50:04.860 --> 00:50:07.890
They sunk.
But where are Zoro and Sanji?

00:50:07.980 --> 00:50:10.010
Oh yeah.
Hey guys.

00:50:13.180 --> 00:50:14.810
Good thing
I got you guys out in time.

00:50:14.900 --> 00:50:16.410
What took you so long?

00:50:16.500 --> 00:50:18.370
- Really.
- Come on, give me a break!

00:50:20.220 --> 00:50:22.130
Food is delicious!

00:50:24.700 --> 00:50:25.920
Hey.

00:50:26.020 --> 00:50:27.650
Aren't you gonna eat?

00:50:28.180 --> 00:50:29.370
There's food for you too.

00:50:32.060 --> 00:50:33.970
Are you guys always like that?

00:50:34.580 --> 00:50:37.650
You said
not to take life too lightly!

00:50:37.740 --> 00:50:40.770
But you do
all those dangerous stuff!

00:50:40.860 --> 00:50:42.850
You could have easily died!

00:50:43.180 --> 00:50:45.330
It was dangerous, wasn't it?

00:50:45.420 --> 00:50:46.930
What's so funny?

00:50:47.020 --> 00:50:48.340
Aren't you afraid to die?

00:50:48.420 --> 00:50:49.850
- Of course.
- Then why?

00:50:51.220 --> 00:50:55.370
A pirate saved my life
when I was a kid.

00:50:56.060 --> 00:50:58.730
He lost an arm doing it.

00:50:59.340 --> 00:51:01.930
<i>It's only an arm...</i>

00:51:02.020 --> 00:51:03.930
<i>I'm glad you're safe.</i>

00:51:04.300 --> 00:51:07.450
So I'll never take life lightly.

00:51:07.580 --> 00:51:09.730
But I have a dream.

00:51:09.820 --> 00:51:12.170
Something I wanna do...
really badly.

00:51:12.620 --> 00:51:15.180
It's not an easy thing to pull off.

00:51:15.260 --> 00:51:18.050
But I'm determined to do it.

00:51:18.780 --> 00:51:21.890
So it's okay if I die trying to do it.

00:51:25.820 --> 00:51:26.850
What is that nose of yours?

00:51:26.940 --> 00:51:28.370
- Nose?
- Yeah, your nose!

00:51:28.460 --> 00:51:29.570
Why is it so long?

00:51:29.660 --> 00:51:31.290
You know what snail is?

00:51:31.380 --> 00:51:32.370
What's that got to do
with anything?

00:51:43.620 --> 00:51:45.450
Captain, we're going down!

00:51:45.580 --> 00:51:47.570
- Let's get out of here!
- How can this be?

00:51:47.660 --> 00:51:48.690
Captain!

00:51:49.500 --> 00:51:53.810
This is Partia?
The goal?!

00:52:03.380 --> 00:52:05.010
What's this...?

00:52:06.460 --> 00:52:10.010
A marine corps base!

00:52:10.820 --> 00:52:12.930
- Are they all down?
- Yes, sir.

00:52:13.740 --> 00:52:14.880
There's one more
in the back.

00:52:14.980 --> 00:52:16.050
Another one?

00:52:16.140 --> 00:52:18.010
What's going on today?

00:52:18.460 --> 00:52:19.600
Nami-san, what's going on?

00:52:19.700 --> 00:52:21.210
But this is it!

00:52:21.300 --> 00:52:22.930
The needle points here.

00:52:23.020 --> 00:52:26.410
Maybe we've got
the wrong Eternal Pose in the first place.

00:52:34.060 --> 00:52:36.850
I knew something wasn't right.

00:52:36.940 --> 00:52:39.050
Gusparday must have set it up.

00:52:39.180 --> 00:52:40.400
Luffy?

00:52:40.500 --> 00:52:44.050
It's just like him
to do something dirty like this.

00:52:44.300 --> 00:52:46.570
How do you know that?

00:52:46.660 --> 00:52:48.410
- I'm sure of it.
- Hey but...

00:52:48.500 --> 00:52:49.770
I think he's right.

00:52:51.220 --> 00:52:52.650
The other day...

00:52:52.740 --> 00:52:55.730
I saw a whole bunch of
Eternal Pose on the ship.

00:52:55.820 --> 00:52:57.040
That's probably one of them.

00:52:57.340 --> 00:52:59.900
A pirate selling out fellow pirates.

00:52:59.980 --> 00:53:01.330
Some kind of General...

00:53:01.420 --> 00:53:02.810
That scum!

00:53:02.900 --> 00:53:04.730
What should we do?
Go after him?

00:53:04.820 --> 00:53:07.250
But we need
the real Eternal Pose.

00:53:07.340 --> 00:53:08.730
Yeah. It's too late.

00:53:08.820 --> 00:53:10.370
Everything's too late!

00:53:11.900 --> 00:53:13.610
Too late for Grandpa.

00:53:13.700 --> 00:53:15.450
Your grandfather?

00:53:16.220 --> 00:53:18.090
Not my real one.

00:53:18.180 --> 00:53:20.690
But he saved my life.

00:53:20.780 --> 00:53:21.850
He's sick, but...

00:53:21.940 --> 00:53:24.850
they won't give him any medicine,
saying he's not a real crew member.

00:53:24.940 --> 00:53:26.410
So I...

00:53:27.580 --> 00:53:29.770
You came here
to get money for the medicine...

00:53:30.020 --> 00:53:31.130
Yeah...

00:53:32.020 --> 00:53:33.010
You stupid or what?

00:53:34.060 --> 00:53:38.250
Your grandpa didn't save your life
so you can do this.

00:53:38.980 --> 00:53:40.570
Yeah but...

00:53:40.980 --> 00:53:43.360
If you know that,
you got to stay alive.

00:53:43.460 --> 00:53:46.290
If you're determined enough
to put your life on the line, that is.

00:53:46.580 --> 00:53:49.220
Why don't you just get him off the ship?!

00:53:49.300 --> 00:53:50.690
You haven't even tried...

00:53:50.780 --> 00:53:53.130
so stop talking like
you know everything!

00:53:53.940 --> 00:53:55.050
Luffy...

00:53:55.140 --> 00:53:57.210
You don't have to...

00:53:57.300 --> 00:53:59.290
tell me that...

00:53:59.380 --> 00:54:01.090
Then good.

00:54:02.300 --> 00:54:04.970
I'm gonna go
kick his butt right now.

00:54:05.060 --> 00:54:06.450
- Wanna come?
- Yes!

00:54:06.580 --> 00:54:07.800
Take me with you!

00:54:08.180 --> 00:54:09.450
Deal.

00:54:10.700 --> 00:54:11.970
All right...

00:54:12.060 --> 00:54:14.440
And we can't just let 300 million berries
slip through our fingers.

00:54:14.860 --> 00:54:17.290
We have to go get the real Eternal Pose.

00:54:17.980 --> 00:54:19.010
Um...

00:54:19.100 --> 00:54:22.730
It sounds like
we're going head to head with Gusparday...

00:54:22.820 --> 00:54:24.290
They're shooting at us!

00:54:25.140 --> 00:54:27.170
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

00:54:27.260 --> 00:54:28.400
<i>Balloon!</i>

00:54:32.060 --> 00:54:33.650
Let's get going!

00:54:33.740 --> 00:54:35.250
Wait a minute!

00:54:35.340 --> 00:54:36.370
How do we know where to go?

00:54:36.460 --> 00:54:37.450
Chopper's nose!

00:54:37.580 --> 00:54:39.130
- Okay!
- Great.

00:54:39.220 --> 00:54:41.050
- You're kidding, right?!
- Don't worry about it.

00:54:41.140 --> 00:54:42.610
And leave everything else
to the navigator.

00:54:42.700 --> 00:54:43.890
Are you guys always like this?

00:54:43.980 --> 00:54:46.170
Yeah, most of the time.

00:55:04.500 --> 00:55:05.970
What are you trying to do?

00:55:08.700 --> 00:55:11.810
I won't let you touch that.

00:55:12.980 --> 00:55:15.620
You're too weak.
But loyal to the end, I see.

00:55:15.700 --> 00:55:17.020
You must be joking.

00:55:17.100 --> 00:55:19.480
I just love that boiler.

00:55:19.780 --> 00:55:21.770
It has nothing
to do with that scum.

00:55:21.860 --> 00:55:24.130
You can't talk about him like that,
can you?

00:55:24.220 --> 00:55:25.610
You work for him.

00:55:25.900 --> 00:55:27.330
I take care of the boiler.

00:55:27.420 --> 00:55:28.930
I'm NOT a pirate!

00:55:29.020 --> 00:55:30.450
You're one strange old man.

00:55:30.580 --> 00:55:32.610
You're one to talk, new one.

00:55:32.980 --> 00:55:35.970
You also don't look like you care
a whole lot about that scum.

00:55:38.340 --> 00:55:39.890
Give me a hand.

00:55:40.340 --> 00:55:43.130
Hurry up.
An old man is asking you to give him a hand.

00:55:48.380 --> 00:55:50.810
I don't care who you are...

00:55:50.900 --> 00:55:52.650
but you aren't doing anything to this.

00:55:52.740 --> 00:55:54.090
All right, all right.

00:55:55.020 --> 00:55:58.490
I wasn't gonna do it to wreck this ship
which I haven't seen in a long time...

00:55:59.500 --> 00:56:01.770
I just wanted to start a commotion.

00:56:03.220 --> 00:56:05.170
To give me a chance to kill him!

00:56:05.700 --> 00:56:07.330
He's very cautious.

00:56:07.420 --> 00:56:08.930
You need to do more than that.

00:56:12.420 --> 00:56:15.450
I see,
you wanna kill Gusparday, do you?

00:56:15.580 --> 00:56:17.690
If I wasn't so sick,

00:56:17.780 --> 00:56:19.570
I'd love to give you a hand.

00:56:21.740 --> 00:56:23.850
You all right?
Doesn't seem like it...

00:56:25.100 --> 00:56:26.930
I can't die just yet.

00:56:27.020 --> 00:56:28.610
Not before
I have my last look at Badger.

00:56:28.700 --> 00:56:29.730
Badger?

00:56:29.820 --> 00:56:31.090
My assistant.

00:56:31.180 --> 00:56:34.570
Went out to kill
a pirate for this old dog.

00:56:35.420 --> 00:56:37.570
That Gusparday.

00:56:37.820 --> 00:56:41.410
He gave the kid a Gun.

00:56:44.060 --> 00:56:45.650
That kid...

00:56:45.860 --> 00:56:47.650
- You saw him?
- We passed each other.

00:56:48.060 --> 00:56:50.490
He was holding a gun
with shaky hands.

00:56:50.620 --> 00:56:51.840
He's probably dead by now.

00:56:51.940 --> 00:56:53.010
Shut up!

00:56:53.100 --> 00:56:54.850
He's not dead!

00:56:54.940 --> 00:56:57.970
Pirates are really good people at heart.

00:56:58.060 --> 00:57:00.210
Gusparday isn't a real pirate.

00:57:00.300 --> 00:57:02.570
No real pirate would kill a small child.

00:57:02.660 --> 00:57:03.690
Gusparday is just...

00:57:03.780 --> 00:57:04.970
That child is...

00:57:05.500 --> 00:57:06.570
still alive.

00:57:06.660 --> 00:57:11.010
At least all the pirates
that I've seen are the same.

00:57:11.100 --> 00:57:14.880
They don't give a second thought about
taking away what's dear to people.

00:57:17.220 --> 00:57:18.210
New Face, you...?

00:57:19.580 --> 00:57:21.770
- I've seen you before...
- I haven't seen you.

00:57:21.860 --> 00:57:23.730
You said you haven't seen
this ship in a long time.

00:57:23.820 --> 00:57:24.850
What do you mean by that?

00:57:25.420 --> 00:57:28.130
You're not here
to just kill Gusparday.

00:57:28.220 --> 00:57:31.690
- You want revenge?
- No, but really.

00:57:31.780 --> 00:57:32.770
Who ARE you?

00:57:32.860 --> 00:57:35.370
A sick old man
shouldn't get so excited.

00:57:35.460 --> 00:57:37.730
I had never seen a steamboat before.

00:57:37.820 --> 00:57:39.370
I was interested.

00:57:39.900 --> 00:57:41.690
My dad used to make boats...

00:57:41.780 --> 00:57:43.930
and I was born in a shipbuilding town.

00:57:44.420 --> 00:57:49.440
My sister and I went to the harbour
to see this when it docked for repairs.

00:57:50.060 --> 00:57:52.290
Then
Gusparday appeared.

00:57:52.380 --> 00:57:53.600
It was 8 years ago.

00:57:57.220 --> 00:57:59.680
There weren't even 100 survivors.

00:57:59.900 --> 00:58:01.810
I've been on my own since then.

00:58:01.900 --> 00:58:04.730
Weren't there other means of survival?

00:58:04.820 --> 00:58:06.970
I see how you must have suffered,
but revenge is...

00:58:07.060 --> 00:58:08.200
What do you know?!

00:58:10.100 --> 00:58:11.320
Forget it.

00:58:11.980 --> 00:58:13.970
It has nothing to do with you.

00:58:15.180 --> 00:58:16.730
And it's too late anyway.

00:58:16.820 --> 00:58:19.330
I've shed a lot of other people's blood.

00:58:19.900 --> 00:58:23.050
I've become good at killing.
I've conned many.

00:58:23.660 --> 00:58:26.410
But I want to end this kind of life
once and for all.

00:58:26.700 --> 00:58:28.250
I'm gonna borrow this.

00:58:28.340 --> 00:58:29.770
You fool...

00:58:29.860 --> 00:58:31.450
As long as you're alive...
If you are alive...

00:58:31.580 --> 00:58:32.930
Old man.

00:58:33.020 --> 00:58:34.690
It's too late.

00:58:35.860 --> 00:58:36.890
See ya.

00:58:36.980 --> 00:58:38.770
I hope your Badger is still alive.

00:58:38.860 --> 00:58:40.410
New Face,

00:58:40.540 --> 00:58:42.170
what's your name?

00:58:43.300 --> 00:58:44.690
Shryer...

00:58:45.100 --> 00:58:46.970
Shryer Bascudo...

00:59:01.780 --> 00:59:04.010
Shryer!!

00:59:07.100 --> 00:59:09.250
Adele!!

00:59:14.140 --> 00:59:17.530
Hurry up, bounty hunter.

00:59:23.180 --> 00:59:25.770
Come play with me.

00:59:34.300 --> 00:59:37.090
I'll take you on whenever you like.

00:59:37.180 --> 00:59:39.930
You don't have to be sneaky about it.

00:59:40.420 --> 00:59:42.650
I heard your story.

00:59:42.740 --> 00:59:45.930
I knew you weren't here for the bounty.

00:59:46.540 --> 00:59:48.690
But I commend you
for your efforts for the past 8 years.

00:59:48.780 --> 00:59:50.250
I don't remember you,

00:59:50.340 --> 00:59:52.250
but you can help me kill
some time now.

00:59:54.620 --> 00:59:57.130
But...

00:59:57.220 --> 01:00:00.920
Needles here
wants to take care of you personally.

01:00:01.020 --> 01:00:03.210
So I'm going to let him.
I'll watch.

01:00:04.300 --> 01:00:06.370
It's just a matter of which of you dies first.

01:00:13.660 --> 01:00:15.730
You're my target too!

01:00:31.260 --> 01:00:33.900
Hey, don't wreck the ship.

01:00:38.180 --> 01:00:39.570
There goes one hand.

01:01:10.940 --> 01:01:12.770
I told you not to wreck the ship

01:01:26.780 --> 01:01:27.810
Are you okay?!

01:01:27.900 --> 01:01:29.250
Can you hear me?

01:01:29.980 --> 01:01:31.330
Hey!

01:01:31.900 --> 01:01:32.930
She coughed up water

01:01:33.020 --> 01:01:34.210
but still...

01:01:36.300 --> 01:01:38.250
It's the General's order.

01:01:38.860 --> 01:01:40.650
Loot everything!

01:01:41.140 --> 01:01:43.810
Burn down and Kill them all!

01:01:52.580 --> 01:01:53.800
Brother...

01:01:56.300 --> 01:01:57.810
Look at this!

01:01:58.420 --> 01:02:00.800
This is a rare ship.

01:02:00.900 --> 01:02:03.130
We'll keep this for the General.

01:02:04.540 --> 01:02:06.650
And the boiler man too.

01:02:17.860 --> 01:02:20.420
Now it's your turn.

01:02:22.020 --> 01:02:24.050
I'm going to kill him.

01:02:24.140 --> 01:02:25.330
He's mine.

01:02:25.420 --> 01:02:26.770
You psycho.

01:02:34.940 --> 01:02:36.160
DIE!

01:02:42.860 --> 01:02:44.250
You're finished!

01:02:57.620 --> 01:02:58.610
See ya.

01:03:25.180 --> 01:03:26.530
Look! Over there!

01:03:43.420 --> 01:03:46.250
He stopped the paddle.

01:03:46.340 --> 01:03:48.570
The boiler's gonna blow any minute!

01:03:49.660 --> 01:03:50.650
New Face...

01:03:50.740 --> 01:03:51.880
Is he going to...

01:04:06.980 --> 01:04:08.250
There he is!

01:04:08.540 --> 01:04:10.170
The Ame Ame Fruit power.

01:04:10.780 --> 01:04:13.970
Guns... Knives...
Nothing can hurt our captain.

01:04:15.540 --> 01:04:16.760
You're a freak!

01:04:26.820 --> 01:04:28.610
He's dead.

01:04:36.100 --> 01:04:38.410
Come on.
That's all you've got?!

01:04:39.220 --> 01:04:41.930
I thought you'd be
more fun than this.

01:04:42.140 --> 01:04:45.410
You're worse than a toy.

01:04:47.820 --> 01:04:49.010
Get out of here!

01:04:53.980 --> 01:04:55.730
I'll squash you.

01:04:58.660 --> 01:04:59.730
Loser!

01:05:02.060 --> 01:05:05.810
GUS... PAR... AAA... DAY!!!

01:05:16.980 --> 01:05:18.810
Who's that?!
Was it his yell?

01:05:18.900 --> 01:05:20.450
- A survivor of the race?
- Who cares!

01:05:20.580 --> 01:05:22.050
Blow 'em away with the cannons!

01:05:22.300 --> 01:05:24.730
He really did get us here with his nose.

01:05:24.940 --> 01:05:26.530
Hey!
You didn't trust me?!

01:05:26.620 --> 01:05:28.130
Their paddle isn't moving.

01:05:28.220 --> 01:05:30.250
It seems like
a lot has happened to them too.

01:05:30.340 --> 01:05:31.410
Luffy!

01:05:31.500 --> 01:05:33.010
We'll leave the rest up to you!

01:05:33.100 --> 01:05:34.090
Thanks.

01:05:36.220 --> 01:05:39.210
<i>Gum-Gum...</i>

01:05:39.380 --> 01:05:42.130
<i>Pistol!!!</i>

01:05:43.580 --> 01:05:44.900
Haaaah!

01:05:45.100 --> 01:05:47.610
<i>Rocket!!</i>

01:05:55.860 --> 01:05:56.930
What's going on?!

01:06:09.700 --> 01:06:11.330
- We caught up with you.
- Who is he?!

01:06:11.420 --> 01:06:13.570
The rubber man we saw in Hannabal!

01:06:13.660 --> 01:06:14.800
Not him again!
Get him!

01:06:16.780 --> 01:06:18.450
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

01:06:20.700 --> 01:06:22.530
<i>Whip!</i>

01:06:30.700 --> 01:06:32.810
They're already going at it.

01:06:33.540 --> 01:06:34.860
You know where to go, right?

01:06:34.940 --> 01:06:37.250
Yeah.
This guy has no sense of direction.

01:06:37.340 --> 01:06:38.480
Shut up, man!

01:06:38.580 --> 01:06:41.650
I'll back you up,
so you guys go do your jobs.

01:06:41.740 --> 01:06:43.290
What are you?
The boss?

01:06:44.100 --> 01:06:46.090
I'm surprised you found us.

01:06:46.180 --> 01:06:48.820
You're living up to
your 30 million-berry bounty.

01:06:49.180 --> 01:06:51.130
So?
What do you want?

01:06:51.220 --> 01:06:54.290
You wanna end up like him too?

01:06:55.060 --> 01:06:57.290
Hmm?
What are YOU doing here?

01:06:57.620 --> 01:07:00.130
He came for my head.

01:07:00.220 --> 01:07:03.410
He did...show me a good time.

01:07:05.700 --> 01:07:06.810
You want to say something?

01:07:06.900 --> 01:07:08.170
Why did you do something like that?

01:07:08.260 --> 01:07:09.730
Like what?

01:07:09.820 --> 01:07:11.450
Oh, the marine corps base.

01:07:11.580 --> 01:07:13.530
Anything goes in this race.

01:07:13.620 --> 01:07:15.890
I did nothing wrong.

01:07:15.980 --> 01:07:17.570
You're good, aren't you?

01:07:17.660 --> 01:07:21.410
You don't need to play
a dirty trick like that.

01:07:21.540 --> 01:07:22.810
I can do whatever I want.

01:07:22.900 --> 01:07:24.850
It's just a game.

01:07:24.940 --> 01:07:25.970
A Same?

01:07:26.060 --> 01:07:27.530
Yeah.
A game.

01:07:27.980 --> 01:07:29.770
I need to play games
for some excitement.

01:07:29.860 --> 01:07:33.010
Or else I'll die of boredom
here on the seas.

01:07:33.700 --> 01:07:37.170
Pirates are a bunch of
losers who just dream big.

01:07:37.260 --> 01:07:38.730
Hidden treasure?

01:07:38.820 --> 01:07:40.730
Wild adventure?

01:07:40.820 --> 01:07:42.850
Who gives a damn about any of those?!

01:07:42.940 --> 01:07:45.650
What's really important is power!

01:07:45.740 --> 01:07:48.380
With power, anything is possible!

01:07:48.460 --> 01:07:51.020
I thought I'd get rid of the idiots...

01:07:51.100 --> 01:07:54.250
who don't realise that.

01:07:54.340 --> 01:07:58.690
The entries increased
when I tripled the prize money this year.

01:07:58.780 --> 01:08:00.810
If anyone survived the race,

01:08:00.900 --> 01:08:03.650
I was going to let
him work for me, as a reward.

01:08:04.260 --> 01:08:06.330
It was that kind of game.

01:08:06.660 --> 01:08:09.120
It's perfect for killing time.

01:08:09.220 --> 01:08:10.330
I get it...

01:08:10.700 --> 01:08:11.730
So...

01:08:11.820 --> 01:08:12.850
you teamed up with that bookie.

01:08:12.940 --> 01:08:14.370
<i>- Hey let me down</i>
- <i>He's</i> ..

01:08:14.460 --> 01:08:15.780
- Off the island by now...
- Wait a <i>second!</i>

01:08:16.020 --> 01:08:17.160
<i>Grandpa!</i>

01:08:17.260 --> 01:08:18.330
- ...with all the bet money.
- Grandpa!

01:08:18.660 --> 01:08:20.610
But who knows if he's still alive.

01:08:21.260 --> 01:08:23.090
His Eternal Pose is...

01:08:23.300 --> 01:08:24.650
also phony.

01:08:28.660 --> 01:08:30.410
He tricked us!

01:08:35.380 --> 01:08:39.050
Grandpa!

01:08:40.020 --> 01:08:41.210
Badger!

01:08:42.060 --> 01:08:44.730
I'm so glad you're alive.
You fool...

01:08:46.100 --> 01:08:47.370
I'm sorry...

01:08:48.380 --> 01:08:49.930
Hey!
I came back to save you!

01:08:50.020 --> 01:08:51.010
Save me?

01:08:51.100 --> 01:08:52.240
I came here with pirates.

01:08:52.340 --> 01:08:54.130
They said they'll help us!

01:08:54.660 --> 01:08:55.880
The pirates?

01:08:55.980 --> 01:08:58.090
Yeah.
I'll tell you the details later!

01:08:58.180 --> 01:08:59.890
First let's get out of here!

01:09:00.100 --> 01:09:01.810
They're really strong, these guys.

01:09:01.900 --> 01:09:03.890
They said they'll drop us off
on the next island.

01:09:03.980 --> 01:09:05.650
And there's a doctor too,

01:09:05.740 --> 01:09:07.770
he can take care of you.

01:09:10.860 --> 01:09:11.850
We'll live!

01:09:12.220 --> 01:09:13.850
You always used to say,

01:09:13.940 --> 01:09:15.160
<i>That we'll live!</i>

01:09:15.260 --> 01:09:17.850
Let's get ourselves out of here
and start a new life somewhere!

01:09:18.300 --> 01:09:20.760
At last something good is
really going to happen to us!

01:09:20.860 --> 01:09:23.320
Let's go,
Grandpa!

01:09:24.100 --> 01:09:25.290
Badger...

01:09:26.620 --> 01:09:27.970
All right.

01:09:34.020 --> 01:09:35.770
- Grandpa?
- Mr Swordsman,

01:09:35.860 --> 01:09:38.890
please take this old dog with you too.

01:09:38.980 --> 01:09:40.370
You don't have to ask.

01:09:40.460 --> 01:09:41.450
Get back on our ship.

01:09:41.580 --> 01:09:42.650
Come on, let's go.

01:09:42.740 --> 01:09:45.890
I have to go get something
in the boiler room.

01:09:45.980 --> 01:09:47.730
You go on ahead.

01:09:48.260 --> 01:09:50.010
All right, Mr Swordsman?

01:09:51.580 --> 01:09:53.410
- Sure.
- Grandpa...

01:09:53.540 --> 01:09:54.970
Don't worry!

01:09:55.060 --> 01:09:56.570
I'll be right back.

01:09:57.420 --> 01:09:58.890
Hurry up, okay?

01:10:02.140 --> 01:10:03.330
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

01:10:03.420 --> 01:10:05.530
- I told you to stop it.
- Luffy.

01:10:05.660 --> 01:10:07.250
- We're finished over here!
- Okay.

01:10:07.340 --> 01:10:08.970
What?
You're leaving already?

01:10:09.420 --> 01:10:11.330
You finally caught up with me.

01:10:11.420 --> 01:10:12.930
Why don't you play with me?

01:10:13.020 --> 01:10:14.410
Shut up and fight.

01:10:15.940 --> 01:10:18.170
What are you babbling about?

01:10:18.260 --> 01:10:19.610
You stupid or what?

01:10:19.700 --> 01:10:22.050
I don't want to play your game,

01:10:22.140 --> 01:10:25.570
and I'm not interested in
what you have to say.

01:10:26.260 --> 01:10:27.690
All I want is..

01:10:27.780 --> 01:10:29.730
To blow you away!

01:10:31.220 --> 01:10:32.730
Nami-san,
I'm finished.

01:10:32.820 --> 01:10:34.290
Then hurry up and come back!

01:10:34.380 --> 01:10:35.600
Something's funny.

01:10:36.100 --> 01:10:37.730
- What?
- The weather.

01:10:37.820 --> 01:10:38.890
I have a bad feeling about this.

01:10:39.620 --> 01:10:40.730
What is it...?

01:10:40.820 --> 01:10:42.730
I know I've felt this before...

01:10:47.140 --> 01:10:48.890
If you're not gonna start,
I will.

01:10:50.060 --> 01:10:51.570
I thought I told you.

01:10:51.660 --> 01:10:55.290
If you don't stop being a smart-ass,
you will die!

01:10:56.980 --> 01:10:58.120
Stop.

01:10:58.220 --> 01:10:59.250
You...

01:10:59.340 --> 01:11:00.850
I get to go first.

01:11:00.940 --> 01:11:02.050
Stand back.

01:11:02.620 --> 01:11:03.840
Come on.
Let's finish this.

01:11:04.380 --> 01:11:06.530
What can a broken toy do?

01:11:06.620 --> 01:11:07.840
I'M GOING TO KILL YOU!

01:11:08.060 --> 01:11:09.810
I've lived this past 8 years...

01:11:09.900 --> 01:11:13.450
just waiting for the chance
to get back at you.

01:11:13.580 --> 01:11:15.450
You killed everyone...

01:11:15.580 --> 01:11:17.130
my sister, my parents, and all my friends!

01:11:17.220 --> 01:11:19.600
I know what I'm doing is pointless,

01:11:19.700 --> 01:11:23.050
but I shed a lot of blood just to get here.

01:11:23.900 --> 01:11:27.250
I'm gonna make you pay for all this,

01:11:27.340 --> 01:11:29.330
Mr General.

01:11:29.420 --> 01:11:31.450
That what I call STUPID.

01:11:33.700 --> 01:11:35.570
Say whatever you want.

01:11:35.660 --> 01:11:38.330
If you can do so...

01:11:38.420 --> 01:11:39.450
Sorry.

01:11:44.980 --> 01:11:46.050
You're in my way.

01:11:48.780 --> 01:11:50.250
Why did he do that?

01:11:51.420 --> 01:11:52.770
He really was in the way.

01:11:52.860 --> 01:11:54.290
You're one spunky kid.

01:11:54.380 --> 01:11:56.840
A smart ass all right,
but I like you.

01:11:57.220 --> 01:11:59.250
Don't make me repeat myself.

01:12:00.060 --> 01:12:01.770
Stop talking and fight!

01:12:03.580 --> 01:12:04.770
Shut ...your...

01:12:05.300 --> 01:12:06.690
mouth!

01:12:14.060 --> 01:12:15.570
Gross!
What's this?

01:12:15.660 --> 01:12:19.050
The Devil's Fruit I ate is
the Ame Ame Fruit.

01:12:19.140 --> 01:12:23.690
I can turn
any part of my body into sugar syrup.

01:12:24.740 --> 01:12:26.850
It doesn't matter...

01:12:26.940 --> 01:12:28.650
how strong your punches are.

01:12:29.780 --> 01:12:31.650
It's showtime.

01:12:37.220 --> 01:12:38.250
How do you like this?

01:12:38.340 --> 01:12:40.130
Having fun dancing around?

01:12:47.900 --> 01:12:49.890
- Oh my God...
- Don't.

01:12:50.340 --> 01:12:51.660
It's his fight.

01:12:51.740 --> 01:12:53.330
He's not gonna like it
if you butt in.

01:12:53.420 --> 01:12:56.010
But...
That candy guy is really strong.

01:12:57.940 --> 01:12:59.370
Hmm...
I'll be right back.

01:13:01.980 --> 01:13:04.440
What's wrong?
Are you full already?

01:13:05.140 --> 01:13:07.810
I still haven't had enough to eat.

01:13:08.180 --> 01:13:10.890
You have to at least show me a good time
like Shryer!

01:13:14.940 --> 01:13:15.970
I see that you will.

01:13:16.420 --> 01:13:19.330
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

01:13:21.420 --> 01:13:22.850
Scared me!

01:13:23.100 --> 01:13:24.370
<i>Bell!</i>

01:13:27.980 --> 01:13:29.170
It's no use.

01:13:29.420 --> 01:13:32.090
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

01:13:32.740 --> 01:13:34.330
<i>Axe!!</i>

01:13:35.980 --> 01:13:37.770
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

01:13:37.940 --> 01:13:39.130
<i>Chomp Chomp!</i>

01:13:43.860 --> 01:13:45.570
Stop being a clown!

01:13:47.620 --> 01:13:49.730
Don't you realise what's happening here?

01:13:49.820 --> 01:13:50.890
Get serious.

01:13:50.980 --> 01:13:52.200
I'm always serious.

01:13:52.300 --> 01:13:53.490
That was serious?

01:13:53.580 --> 01:13:55.130
I got myself out, didn't I?

01:13:55.580 --> 01:13:57.250
You smart ass!

01:14:00.140 --> 01:14:01.130
Hey.

01:14:01.220 --> 01:14:03.860
Are you going to
leave your treasure there like that?

01:14:04.900 --> 01:14:09.210
Needles almost stepped on it,
and you were really upset.

01:14:09.300 --> 01:14:13.410
It's the precious hat that
Red Hair Shanks gave you, isn't it?

01:14:16.180 --> 01:14:17.570
He didn't give it to me.

01:14:17.660 --> 01:14:19.850
I'm keeping it for him!
Don't touch it!

01:14:19.940 --> 01:14:22.580
Try and get it,
if you want it back so badly.

01:14:22.660 --> 01:14:23.770
Stop!

01:14:23.860 --> 01:14:25.730
I'll kill you if you do anything to it!

01:14:25.820 --> 01:14:27.040
You can't protect it...

01:14:27.140 --> 01:14:28.850
just by talk!

01:14:29.060 --> 01:14:30.280
STOP!

01:14:34.430 --> 01:14:36.880
Damn you!

01:14:38.940 --> 01:14:40.290
<i>Keep this for me.</i>

01:14:40.380 --> 01:14:42.410
<i>I'll wait for you to come return it to me</i>

01:14:42.540 --> 01:14:44.290
<i>when you're a real pirate...</i>

01:14:44.380 --> 01:14:48.810
<i>One day, I'm gonna find One Piece and
become the Pirate King!</i>

01:14:52.940 --> 01:14:55.890
Now are you serious?

01:15:07.060 --> 01:15:08.130
Give it back to me.

01:15:08.860 --> 01:15:11.290
Now you've got a good look in your eyes.

01:15:12.700 --> 01:15:14.050
Fine.

01:15:14.140 --> 01:15:15.170
Take It!!!

01:15:20.660 --> 01:15:22.010
What's going on?

01:15:22.100 --> 01:15:23.850
We can't see anything from here...

01:15:24.380 --> 01:15:26.610
There's something strange
about this weather!

01:15:26.700 --> 01:15:29.080
There's got to be a huge energy.

01:15:31.580 --> 01:15:33.250
A huge energy...

01:15:33.340 --> 01:15:34.330
Like...

01:15:34.860 --> 01:15:36.250
<i>Those sea are</i>

01:15:36.340 --> 01:15:38.610
<i>Known for cyclones.</i>

01:15:42.620 --> 01:15:44.730
Everybody, hurry up!
Get ready to sail!

01:15:44.820 --> 01:15:46.970
There's an island nearby.
We're going there!

01:15:47.060 --> 01:15:48.450
But Sanji and Luffy aren't back yet.

01:15:48.580 --> 01:15:50.330
So we're just getting ready to sail!

01:15:50.820 --> 01:15:52.850
Luffy, you gotta hurry up!

01:15:53.380 --> 01:15:56.370
There's a cyclone on its way.

01:16:11.580 --> 01:16:13.050
I'm sorry.

01:16:14.020 --> 01:16:15.650
It must be difficult for you...

01:16:15.740 --> 01:16:17.170
It's really difficult for me too.

01:16:17.260 --> 01:16:19.210
What are you doing, old man?

01:16:19.900 --> 01:16:21.730
Why are you still here?

01:16:21.820 --> 01:16:25.010
A hang over.
Why are you making all that noise?

01:16:25.220 --> 01:16:28.010
The Straw Hat Pirate is
fighting Gusparday.

01:16:28.940 --> 01:16:31.090
Everyone else is down already.

01:16:31.180 --> 01:16:32.770
You're the only ones left.

01:16:33.300 --> 01:16:35.130
And this ship is going to sink soon.

01:16:35.540 --> 01:16:37.650
You better run while you still can.

01:16:42.780 --> 01:16:43.810
What was that?

01:16:45.260 --> 01:16:46.770
Hey, old man.

01:16:46.860 --> 01:16:47.890
Who's there?!

01:16:47.980 --> 01:16:49.450
Oh, me?

01:16:49.540 --> 01:16:50.730
I'm with the Straw Hat Pirate.

01:16:50.820 --> 01:16:51.960
What are you doing here?

01:16:52.060 --> 01:16:53.250
Get off the ship!

01:16:53.980 --> 01:16:55.300
You better too.

01:16:55.380 --> 01:16:56.520
That kid's waiting for you.

01:16:57.340 --> 01:17:00.250
I'm going to stay.

01:17:00.340 --> 01:17:03.090
I have another dear child here.

01:17:03.180 --> 01:17:06.730
I want to stay with her 'til the end.

01:17:08.340 --> 01:17:10.250
So go, young man.
Hurry.

01:17:10.860 --> 01:17:13.010
I shut all her valves.

01:17:13.100 --> 01:17:15.170
She's gonna blow in a few minutes.

01:17:18.700 --> 01:17:20.810
- Luffy!
- Is he okay?!

01:17:22.780 --> 01:17:24.690
It's for sure heading this way.

01:17:24.780 --> 01:17:25.770
A direct hit.

01:17:26.460 --> 01:17:27.530
You...

01:17:27.620 --> 01:17:29.090
You are tough...

01:17:29.180 --> 01:17:31.290
You still can stand up after all this.

01:17:32.180 --> 01:17:34.450
The storm is getting worse.

01:17:34.580 --> 01:17:36.170
We better finish this.

01:17:36.260 --> 01:17:39.410
I told you I was gonna get you!

01:17:41.180 --> 01:17:43.770
I'm getting sick of your lousy punches.

01:17:44.380 --> 01:17:47.090
But what can I expect from
30 million berries.

01:17:47.180 --> 01:17:52.200
I'm 95 million. Of course
there's no way you can beat me!

01:17:52.580 --> 01:17:54.730
I'll at least give you a painless death.

01:17:55.980 --> 01:17:57.850
I'm being too kind.

01:17:58.940 --> 01:18:00.970
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

01:18:01.940 --> 01:18:04.090
<i>Ikebana!!!</i>

01:18:14.100 --> 01:18:16.090
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

01:18:17.740 --> 01:18:18.880
<i>Spear!</i>

01:18:23.660 --> 01:18:24.850
You finished?

01:18:24.940 --> 01:18:26.610
The ship is about to sink.

01:18:27.100 --> 01:18:28.320
We're leaving now.

01:18:29.580 --> 01:18:31.610
You go ahead.
It'll take a few more minutes.

01:18:32.460 --> 01:18:34.770
That one was pretty good.

01:18:34.860 --> 01:18:38.530
When I'm not sugar syrup,
I have a regular body...

01:18:38.620 --> 01:18:41.610
It's been awhile
since I felt pain like that.

01:18:43.060 --> 01:18:45.370
Normally people would be dead.

01:18:45.980 --> 01:18:48.810
Oh well, we're about to leave,
but we'll be back for you.

01:18:48.900 --> 01:18:50.170
- Have any problems with that?
- No.

01:18:50.260 --> 01:18:52.210
- Here. Take these.
- What are they?

01:18:52.300 --> 01:18:53.650
Use them well.

01:18:53.740 --> 01:18:54.850
We don't have time.

01:18:58.700 --> 01:19:00.450
Sanji!
What took you so long?

01:19:00.580 --> 01:19:02.650
I'll tell you later.
We have to go now!

01:19:02.740 --> 01:19:04.330
It's dangerous here.
I know that.

01:19:04.420 --> 01:19:05.810
Where's Luffy?

01:19:06.140 --> 01:19:07.170
Hey.

01:19:07.260 --> 01:19:09.010
I thought
you were gonna bring the old man.

01:19:09.100 --> 01:19:11.050
He's gonna blow up the boiler.

01:19:11.780 --> 01:19:13.250
In less than a minute.

01:19:22.100 --> 01:19:23.690
Are you kidding?!
Turn back the ship!

01:19:23.780 --> 01:19:25.170
Why didn't you help Grandpa?!

01:19:25.260 --> 01:19:26.250
Why you left him there to die?

01:19:26.340 --> 01:19:27.770
Why did you come back alone?!

01:19:27.980 --> 01:19:30.090
You said you were gonna help us!

01:19:30.180 --> 01:19:31.930
- WHY?
- Where's Luffy?

01:19:32.020 --> 01:19:33.530
He can't come right now.
Later.

01:19:34.980 --> 01:19:36.970
- Zoro!
- It's better for him like this now.

01:19:37.060 --> 01:19:38.380
Why did you do that?

01:19:41.300 --> 01:19:43.130
Didn't you notice?

01:19:43.220 --> 01:19:44.250
Badger is...

01:19:44.340 --> 01:19:46.610
Badger is a girl!!

01:20:24.900 --> 01:20:27.540
Is Luffy all right?!

01:20:27.620 --> 01:20:29.690
- I don't know...
- You don't know?!

01:20:29.780 --> 01:20:31.890
It was a huge explosion!

01:20:31.980 --> 01:20:35.050
Even if he lived through it,
he could be drowning!

01:20:35.140 --> 01:20:36.650
Why did that old man have to...

01:20:36.740 --> 01:20:39.610
There must have been a reason.

01:20:39.700 --> 01:20:41.210
Like what?
What are you talking about?

01:20:41.300 --> 01:20:43.610
Let's go back!
We have to go get Luffy!

01:20:43.700 --> 01:20:45.690
Wait. He's alive.

01:20:47.380 --> 01:20:49.170
So is Gusparday.

01:20:56.660 --> 01:20:58.130
What was that?!

01:20:58.220 --> 01:21:00.170
The ship just exploded!

01:21:00.740 --> 01:21:02.210
How come?!

01:21:02.300 --> 01:21:04.090
Where's that jerk?

01:21:04.180 --> 01:21:05.290
Did he drown?

01:21:05.700 --> 01:21:07.020
I'm here.

01:21:07.780 --> 01:21:09.250
Still here, huh?!

01:21:15.420 --> 01:21:18.130
Look what just happened to my ship.

01:21:18.220 --> 01:21:20.810
It was my favourite.

01:21:22.220 --> 01:21:24.130
Your men must have done it.

01:21:24.220 --> 01:21:25.210
They're not my men.

01:21:25.300 --> 01:21:26.290
They're my friends.

01:21:27.180 --> 01:21:29.450
They're my friends on the ship.

01:21:30.540 --> 01:21:33.930
Listen to you.

01:21:34.020 --> 01:21:36.250
You're a pirate. Pirates don't play house.

01:21:36.340 --> 01:21:37.410
Don't be a fool!

01:21:37.540 --> 01:21:41.730
On the high seas,
you either dominate or are dominated.

01:21:41.820 --> 01:21:43.570
Power is everything!

01:21:43.660 --> 01:21:45.970
That's why I quit the marine
and became a pirate.

01:21:46.060 --> 01:21:50.850
I hate the ocean,
but it was the surest way to get power.

01:21:53.020 --> 01:21:55.730
That's why you're a scum ball!

01:21:56.700 --> 01:21:58.770
You don't know what's genuine.

01:21:58.860 --> 01:22:01.240
That's why you can talk like that.

01:22:01.340 --> 01:22:04.610
You have no pride,
no faith in your friends.

01:22:04.700 --> 01:22:07.570
You're not worth
that pirate flag you raise!

01:22:07.660 --> 01:22:10.040
I'm gonna bust open
that big head of yours.

01:22:11.180 --> 01:22:12.290
Just to kill time.

01:22:14.540 --> 01:22:16.050
Sounds interesting.

01:22:16.260 --> 01:22:19.730
No one has ever talked to me like that.

01:22:19.820 --> 01:22:23.700
To respect you for your boldness,
I'll see this fight until the end.

01:22:24.220 --> 01:22:25.330
You see,

01:22:25.420 --> 01:22:27.980
There's an emergency boat under the deck.

01:22:28.580 --> 01:22:30.090
And there's that.

01:22:31.980 --> 01:22:34.330
Oh my God!
What's that?

01:22:34.860 --> 01:22:36.180
A storm.

01:22:36.260 --> 01:22:38.820
A sinking ship and a cyclone.

01:22:38.900 --> 01:22:43.330
A perfect condition for us who ate the
Devil's Fruit and can't swim.

01:22:43.420 --> 01:22:44.930
It's simple.

01:22:45.580 --> 01:22:47.850
Only the winner lives.

01:22:48.140 --> 01:22:50.650
You ready?!

01:22:55.820 --> 01:22:57.250
I got you now.

01:22:57.340 --> 01:22:58.810
You wanna go dancing...

01:23:05.420 --> 01:23:07.170
Why?

01:23:07.260 --> 01:23:10.210
Why didn't his hands stick?

01:23:15.060 --> 01:23:16.730
What's this powder?

01:23:16.820 --> 01:23:17.850
Flour?!

01:23:22.140 --> 01:23:24.450
Now that I won't get stuck,
this fight is mine!

01:23:25.300 --> 01:23:26.370
Let's go!

01:23:27.140 --> 01:23:28.810
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

01:23:28.900 --> 01:23:31.850
<i>Gatling!!!</i>

01:23:42.260 --> 01:23:45.530
You're the one
pretending to be a pirate, Gusparday!

01:23:46.540 --> 01:23:48.290
But now it's over!!

01:23:50.140 --> 01:23:52.330
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

01:23:53.060 --> 01:23:54.810
<i>Bow... Gun!!</i>

01:24:01.620 --> 01:24:03.890
We're not finished yet,
Straw Hat!

01:24:04.100 --> 01:24:05.210
Now it's my turn!

01:24:05.780 --> 01:24:07.810
I'll skewer you!

01:24:10.940 --> 01:24:12.810
<i>Gum-Gum</i>

01:24:12.900 --> 01:24:13.890
<i>You fool!</i>

01:24:13.980 --> 01:24:15.370
Can't you see these spikes...

01:24:17.740 --> 01:24:21.010
<i>Bazookaaaa...</i>

01:24:41.180 --> 01:24:45.010
When he's hard candy,
I can blow him away...

01:24:45.100 --> 01:24:46.770
l win.

01:24:48.700 --> 01:24:50.090
Serves him right.

01:24:56.300 --> 01:24:58.010
It's really a direct hit.

01:24:58.100 --> 01:25:00.770
Luffy...
It's taking him too long.

01:25:00.860 --> 01:25:03.170
He'd better hurry up or it'll be too late.

01:25:03.260 --> 01:25:04.890
Don't panic.

01:25:05.220 --> 01:25:06.890
Aren't you worried?!

01:25:07.460 --> 01:25:10.650
He's always managed
to get through things like this.

01:25:12.820 --> 01:25:14.970
We gotta believe in our captain.

01:25:35.340 --> 01:25:36.970
This must be a joke.

01:25:37.660 --> 01:25:38.880
I'm alive.

01:25:38.980 --> 01:25:40.610
It's not a joke.

01:25:43.060 --> 01:25:45.810
Old Man,
what are all those for?

01:25:45.900 --> 01:25:48.330
I was trying hard to stay alive.

01:25:48.420 --> 01:25:52.370
In any case, it was really difficult
trying to carry out 2 grown men.

01:25:54.140 --> 01:25:55.170
Straw Hat!

01:25:55.260 --> 01:25:56.580
One hell of a lad.

01:25:56.660 --> 01:25:58.850
He beat that Gusparday.

01:26:02.620 --> 01:26:05.690
Then there was no reason
for you to save me.

01:26:06.420 --> 01:26:08.170
There's no reason for me to stay alive.

01:26:08.860 --> 01:26:12.250
The thought of killing Gusparday was
what kept me going.

01:26:12.860 --> 01:26:15.810
And now this Straw Hat
took that away from me.

01:26:16.460 --> 01:26:19.730
I have no reason
to stay alive anymore...

01:26:21.780 --> 01:26:24.370
I don't agree.

01:26:25.940 --> 01:26:31.250
God can surprise you at times.
What are you talking about?

01:26:31.340 --> 01:26:34.450
You have a big, old scar on your back.

01:26:34.580 --> 01:26:36.130
- You saw it?
- Yes.

01:26:36.220 --> 01:26:38.170
Now I'm sure of it.

01:26:38.260 --> 01:26:40.410
You said you had a little sister...

01:26:40.940 --> 01:26:42.210
Well, she's alive.

01:26:43.900 --> 01:26:45.120
What are you saying?

01:26:45.220 --> 01:26:46.770
She died 8 years ago.

01:26:46.860 --> 01:26:49.890
That day,
I saved a girl from the river.

01:26:49.980 --> 01:26:51.610
She was 3 years old.

01:26:52.380 --> 01:26:54.370
Her name, I remember well.

01:26:55.140 --> 01:26:57.170
Adele Bascudo.

01:26:59.260 --> 01:27:00.890
Grandpa!!

01:27:01.740 --> 01:27:05.010
Grandpa!

01:27:05.820 --> 01:27:07.170
Over here!

01:27:07.260 --> 01:27:10.050
Grandpa!

01:27:12.140 --> 01:27:13.770
Life can be interesting.

01:27:13.860 --> 01:27:15.050
As long as you live,

01:27:15.140 --> 01:27:16.610
Good things are

01:27:16.700 --> 01:27:18.570
bound to happen.

01:27:20.820 --> 01:27:24.090
Thank you so much.
You even gave her clothes to wear.

01:27:24.180 --> 01:27:26.050
They're my old clothes.

01:27:26.140 --> 01:27:28.450
Old Man,
I thought you were ready to die.

01:27:28.580 --> 01:27:29.770
Who me?

01:27:30.060 --> 01:27:31.090
Don't be stupid.

01:27:31.180 --> 01:27:35.610
I only wanted to see the last of my boiler.
I never said I was ready to die.

01:27:43.300 --> 01:27:44.850
Why is the air so heavy?

01:27:44.940 --> 01:27:46.260
What do you expect?

01:27:46.340 --> 01:27:48.530
They just found out about each other...

01:27:49.540 --> 01:27:51.690
- My hat...
- Take it easy...

01:27:51.780 --> 01:27:53.730
We looked everywhere for it.

01:27:53.820 --> 01:27:56.130
- I know how you feel but...
- My hat...

01:27:57.020 --> 01:27:58.010
There.

01:27:58.620 --> 01:28:00.850
My hat!

01:28:02.220 --> 01:28:03.290
You...

01:28:03.380 --> 01:28:05.610
You said it was important to you.

01:28:05.700 --> 01:28:07.570
I just happened to walk past it,
so I picked it up.

01:28:07.660 --> 01:28:10.850
Thank you!
You're a nice guy!

01:28:11.220 --> 01:28:13.680
Nami!
Fix it for me again!

01:28:13.780 --> 01:28:14.920
Yes, yes.

01:28:17.420 --> 01:28:20.370
We're getting close to the island!

01:28:20.700 --> 01:28:22.410
That must be the goal.

01:28:22.540 --> 01:28:25.370
It also matches the log
that Grandpa showed me.

01:28:25.460 --> 01:28:26.780
Which means...

01:28:27.180 --> 01:28:29.290
We WIN!!

01:28:29.540 --> 01:28:31.210
300 million berries!

01:28:32.140 --> 01:28:33.410
Yeah!

01:28:33.540 --> 01:28:35.610
Don't tell me you're being shy.

01:28:35.740 --> 01:28:37.060
No, I'm not.

01:28:37.140 --> 01:28:39.650
It's just that I don't have the right.

01:28:39.740 --> 01:28:41.850
The right? For what?

01:28:42.220 --> 01:28:45.250
I've shed people's blood for my purpose.

01:28:45.340 --> 01:28:47.770
I'm no different from Gusparday
in that sense.

01:28:48.300 --> 01:28:49.290
That's the kind of person I am...

01:28:49.380 --> 01:28:51.840
Is that it?
That's what you were worried about?

01:28:52.100 --> 01:28:55.050
You can think about the past later.

01:28:55.140 --> 01:28:58.210
Now, just think about moving forward.

01:28:59.540 --> 01:29:03.290
See, she's already
trying to take the first step.

01:29:05.580 --> 01:29:08.690
You don't have to rush yourself,
but you have to look ahead.

01:29:08.780 --> 01:29:10.570
Worry about the rest later.

01:29:13.180 --> 01:29:14.690
Marines?!

01:29:14.780 --> 01:29:16.100
Why are they here?!

01:29:16.180 --> 01:29:19.690
They're the ones who were
chasing us the other day.

01:29:20.900 --> 01:29:22.770
We've been waiting for you,
pirates!

01:29:22.860 --> 01:29:24.770
We're going to catch you
and then hang you!

01:29:24.860 --> 01:29:27.570
Major, we have to
put them on trial first.

01:29:27.660 --> 01:29:29.010
I know that!

01:29:29.700 --> 01:29:31.130
Forward, full speed!

01:29:31.220 --> 01:29:32.930
Chase them to the edge of the world!

01:29:33.340 --> 01:29:36.530
In the name of absolute justice!

01:29:37.940 --> 01:29:39.210
Why?!

01:29:39.300 --> 01:29:42.450
You can just tell them
you rescued us.

01:29:42.580 --> 01:29:44.810
They'll never believe us.

01:29:44.900 --> 01:29:46.930
We're pirates!

01:29:47.020 --> 01:29:49.210
We're supposed to flee from them.

01:29:49.300 --> 01:29:50.970
But...
But...

01:29:51.060 --> 01:29:54.610
You stay out of trouble from now on.

01:29:54.700 --> 01:29:56.970
Don't get involved with outlaws.

01:29:58.180 --> 01:29:59.210
But...

01:30:00.140 --> 01:30:02.810
And never again say
there's nothing to live for, all right?

01:30:02.900 --> 01:30:03.890
Bye!

01:30:03.980 --> 01:30:05.170
Take care!

01:30:06.140 --> 01:30:08.050
Grow up to be a nice lady.

01:30:08.860 --> 01:30:11.170
You'll first have to
watch your language.

01:30:11.820 --> 01:30:12.890
Be good.

01:30:12.980 --> 01:30:15.090
Take care of yourself.

01:30:23.460 --> 01:30:25.650
You thought you helped me like that?

01:30:26.420 --> 01:30:27.640
Oh well...

01:30:27.740 --> 01:30:29.890
We'll never see each other again anyway.

01:30:31.340 --> 01:30:33.170
Get out of here, pirate!

01:30:33.260 --> 01:30:34.250
Yeah!

01:30:35.540 --> 01:30:37.610
See ya!

01:30:37.700 --> 01:30:41.580
Take care of yourselves!

01:30:41.900 --> 01:30:44.280
You too!

01:30:44.380 --> 01:30:46.290
All of you!

01:30:46.380 --> 01:30:48.570
Thank you!

01:30:49.060 --> 01:30:50.050
Old Man...

01:30:51.580 --> 01:30:53.810
I don't know how to put it,

01:30:53.900 --> 01:30:57.090
but that one step forward...

01:30:57.180 --> 01:30:59.640
I think I'm ready to take it.

01:30:59.740 --> 01:31:00.730
Right.

01:31:01.860 --> 01:31:04.370
Hey, that ship is turning back.

01:31:04.460 --> 01:31:06.770
So, no winner this year, huh?

01:31:06.860 --> 01:31:09.210
Well, what can you expect with this?

01:31:09.300 --> 01:31:11.170
Whose poor ship is that?

01:31:11.260 --> 01:31:12.250
Let's see...

01:31:12.340 --> 01:31:14.690
The flag is a
skull and crossbones with a straw hat.

01:31:14.780 --> 01:31:17.850
- What? It's HIM!
- Him?!

01:31:17.940 --> 01:31:20.320
Yeah!
He has a huge bounty on his head.

01:31:20.420 --> 01:31:22.530
It just went up recently.

01:31:22.740 --> 01:31:24.330
I think it was 100 million berries.

01:31:24.420 --> 01:31:26.530
That's more than Gusparday!

01:31:27.700 --> 01:31:29.290
- That was unexpected.
- What was?

01:31:29.380 --> 01:31:33.290
I can't believe you just gave up
300 million berries easily.

01:31:34.060 --> 01:31:35.530
We didn't have a choice.

01:31:35.820 --> 01:31:37.770
What else could we have done?!

01:31:38.100 --> 01:31:41.930
That bookie!
It's his fault!

01:31:42.020 --> 01:31:44.930
He was even trying to trick Gusparday!
We have to go get him!!!

01:31:45.020 --> 01:31:47.250
But he may not even be
alive anymore...

01:31:47.340 --> 01:31:48.770
Forget it.

01:31:49.100 --> 01:31:50.570
Cheer up!

01:31:50.660 --> 01:31:54.170
Our journey isn't over yet.
We're in for more adventure.

01:31:54.260 --> 01:31:55.610
That's right, Nami-san.

01:31:55.700 --> 01:31:58.770
And right now,
we have to do something about them.

01:31:59.260 --> 01:32:02.210
Stop! Pirates!!

01:32:02.620 --> 01:32:03.690
Oh boy.

01:32:03.780 --> 01:32:06.010
Why am I stuck on this shabby pirate ship?

01:32:06.100 --> 01:32:08.290
Everyone is
a happy-go-lucky slack off.

01:32:09.100 --> 01:32:11.970
We're gonna outrun those ships
and look for the next island!

01:32:12.060 --> 01:32:13.380
Get to work!

01:32:13.460 --> 01:32:14.600
Yes, Nami-san.

01:32:14.860 --> 01:32:15.850
All right!

01:32:15.940 --> 01:32:19.130
Forward full speed
to becoming the Pirate King!

01:32:19.340 --> 01:32:20.530
The next adventure awaits us!

01:32:20.620 --> 01:32:22.090
I am the only one working hard...

01:32:22.090 --> 01:32:24.090
Let's go, everyone!

01:32:24.420 --> 01:32:26.880
Let's go!

01:32:39.860 --> 01:32:43.130
<i>Me wo tojita sono naka ni mieta </i>

01:32:39.860 --> 01:32:43.130
<i>When I close my eyes</i>

01:32:43.220 --> 01:32:45.530
<i>Kasukana mabushisa wo</i>

01:32:43.220 --> 01:32:45.530
<i>I see sunlight in my eyes</i>

01:32:45.620 --> 01:32:48.050
<i>Tsukamitorou to shita</i>

01:32:45.620 --> 01:32:48.050
<i>try to catch the sunlight...</i>

01:32:48.140 --> 01:32:49.930
<i>Oroka na dori-ma- </i>

01:32:48.140 --> 01:32:49.930
<i>because I am a foolish dreamer</i>

01:32:50.020 --> 01:32:52.450
<i>Nobahsita te ha tojita me ni</i>

01:32:50.020 --> 01:32:52.450
<i>But I can't see my hands</i>

01:32:52.580 --> 01:32:55.610
<i>Utsuranakute tohou ni kureru</i>

01:32:52.580 --> 01:32:55.610
<i>because my eyes are closed</i>

01:32:55.700 --> 01:32:59.850
<i>Shateikyori kara zuibun tooku njimu</i>

01:32:55.700 --> 01:32:59.850
<i>The light seems far and blurred</i>

01:32:59.940 --> 01:33:04.930
<i>Dounika mada boku ha boku wo
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hyamenai de ikiteiru </i>

01:32:59.940 --> 01:33:04.930
<i>I am still alive and being myself</i>

01:33:05.020 --> 01:33:10.890
<i>Tatta ichodo waraeru nara
\hnandodemo naitatte ii ya </i>

01:33:05.020 --> 01:33:10.890
<i>I don't mind crying many times
\h\has long as I can laugh once</i>

01:33:10.980 --> 01:33:14.930
<i>Seiippai unmei ni teikou</i>

01:33:10.980 --> 01:33:14.930
<i>I tried to fight my destiny many times</i>

01:33:15.020 --> 01:33:21.010
<i>\h\h\hSeikai, fuseikai no handan,
jibun dake ni yurusareta kenri </i>

01:33:15.020 --> 01:33:21.010
<i>\h\h\h\hOnly I have the right
to judge right from wrong</i>

01:33:21.100 --> 01:33:25.130
<i>Sailing day, kaji wo tore</i>

01:33:21.100 --> 01:33:25.130
<i>Sailing day, Steer your own ship</i>

01:33:25.220 --> 01:33:29.410
<i>Yoake wo matanai de hoo wo hatta</i>

01:33:25.220 --> 01:33:29.410
<i>Raising a sail before dawn</i>

01:33:29.540 --> 01:33:31.690
<i>Oroka na dori-ma</i>

01:33:29.540 --> 01:33:31.690
<i>because I am a foolish dreamer</i>

01:33:31.780 --> 01:33:37.250
<i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKazoetara kiri ga nai
hodo no kiken ya fuan sae mo</i>

01:33:31.780 --> 01:33:37.250
<i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hI have been through
so many dangers and unsureness</i>

01:33:37.340 --> 01:33:39.850
<i>Aishite mukaeutta</i>

01:33:37.340 --> 01:33:39.850
<i>and I loved them all</i>

01:33:39.940 --> 01:33:41.730
<i>Akireta biri-va-</i>

01:33:39.940 --> 01:33:41.730
<i>because I am a foolish believer</i>

01:33:41.820 --> 01:33:45.050
<i>Me wo hiraita sono saki ni mieru</i>

01:33:41.820 --> 01:33:45.050
<i>When I open my eyes</i>

01:33:45.140 --> 01:33:47.600
<i>Tashika na mabushisa ga </i>

01:33:45.140 --> 01:33:47.600
<i>see the light for sure</i>

01:33:47.700 --> 01:33:51.650
<i>Kara ni natta ha-to ni riyuu wo sosogu</i>

01:33:47.700 --> 01:33:51.650
<i>That light is the reason why
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hHollow my heart</i>

01:33:51.740 --> 01:33:56.760
<i>Sou shite mata boku ha boku no
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hsenaka wo oshiteiku </i>

01:33:51.740 --> 01:33:56.760
<i>\h\h\h\hThis is how
I motivate myself</i>

01:33:56.860 --> 01:34:02.730
<i>Tatta hitotsu wo tsukamu tame
\h\h\h\hikutsu demo ushinaun da </i>

01:33:56.860 --> 01:34:02.730
<i>I don't mind how much I lose to gain
\h\h\h\h\h\h\hone important thing in life</i>

01:34:02.820 --> 01:34:06.850
<i>Seiippai sonzai no shoumei</i>

01:34:02.820 --> 01:34:06.850
<i>This is howl prove my existence</i>

01:34:06.940 --> 01:34:12.770
<i>\h\h\h\h\hAyamachi mo machigai mo
jibun dake ni kachi no aru zaihou</i>

01:34:06.940 --> 01:34:12.770
<i>Failure and mistakes are
valuable treasures to me</i>

01:34:12.860 --> 01:34:16.890
<i>Sailing day kaji wo tore</i>

01:34:12.860 --> 01:34:16.890
<i>Sailing day, steer your own ship</i>

01:34:16.980 --> 01:34:21.250
<i>Arashi no naka ureshisou ni hou wo hatta</i>

01:34:16.980 --> 01:34:21.250
<i>Railing a sail happily in storm</i>

01:34:21.340 --> 01:34:24.210
<i>Oroka na dori-ma-</i>

01:34:21.340 --> 01:34:24.210
<i>because I am a foolish dreamer</i>

01:34:26.300 --> 01:34:29.770
<i>Daremo ga biri-va-</i>

01:34:26.300 --> 01:34:29.770
<i>Everyone is a dreamer</i>

01:34:31.540 --> 01:34:35.170
<i>Eien no dori-ma-</i>

01:34:31.540 --> 01:34:35.170
<i>Forever a dreamer...</i>
